bes, to heat and cool itself.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters bring it up in geothermal, greenhouse and vertical farming threads as a low-tech example of growing citrus in a cold climate.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"geothermal greenhouses\",\"categories\":[\"Environment, agriculture & food systems\",\"Power grid, heating & buildings\",\"Home, DIY & practical skills\"],\"tags\":[\"geothermal\",\"earth tubes\",\"greenhouse\",\"citrus\",\"passive heating\",\"backyard farming\"],\"quote\":\"Really interesting story/concept and I'm hoping to replicate on a small scale\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"ZMQbHMgK2rw\",\"title\":\"The Fastest Maze-Solving Competition On Earth\",\"channel\":\"Veritasium\",\"summary\":\"Veritasium visits the Micromouse competition, where small autonomous robots race to solve mazes at extreme speed. It covers the competition's technical history, including fans and ground effect enabling very high-g turns.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as a nice introduction to micromouse and maze-racing robots.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"micromouse robotics\",\"categories\":[\"Robotics\",\"Mechanical & precision engineering\",\"Embedded systems & DIY electronics\"],\"tags\":[\"micromouse\",\"maze solving\",\"robotics\",\"ground effect\",\"competition\"],\"quote\":\"is a nice introduction to the competition and its technical history.\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"ZPoqNeR3_UA\",\"title\":\"Star Trek TNG Ambient Engine Noise (Idling for 24 hrs)\",\"channel\":\"crysknife007\",\"summary\":\"A 24-hour loop of Star Trek TNG starship engine ambience, meant as background sound for relaxing, sleeping or concentrating.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people use it as background noise for coding and focus, and share it as a personal favorite.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"ambient focus sound\",\"categories\":[\"