ehavior\"],\"tags\":[\"jordan peterson\",\"bible\",\"archetypes\",\"religion\",\"psychology\"],\"quote\":\"You can be a hardline atheist and still get tons of value out of these lectures.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"fCn8zs912OE\",\"title\":\"The Zipf Mystery\",\"channel\":\"Vsauce\",\"summary\":\"Vsauce's explainer on Zipf's law, the pattern in which the frequency of a word is inversely related to its rank. It shows the pattern across many domains and discusses why it remains unexplained.\",\"why_hn\":\"Linked as an entertaining introduction to Zipf's law and power-law distributions.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"zipf's law\",\"categories\":[\"Language & linguistics\",\"Recreational & visual math\"],\"tags\":[\"zipf's law\",\"power laws\",\"word frequency\",\"linguistics\",\"vsauce\"],\"quote\":\"It's actually a very deep question, called the Zipf mystery\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"fNpsgTIpODA\",\"title\":\"Gabriella Gonzalez – How to market Haskell to a mainstream programmer\",\"channel\":\"Konfy\",\"summary\":\"Gabriella Gonzalez argues that developers misunderstand marketing as deception or hype, and applies the technology-adoption ideas of Crossing the Chasm to Haskell. She looks at what keeps Haskell from reaching mainstream programmers and what a community can do about it.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters point to it as a clear take on why functional languages stall outside niches, and its lessons are seen as applying to any technology trying to go mainstream.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"technology adoption\",\"categories\":[\"Functional programming\",\"Software practice, open source & careers\"],\"tags\":[\"haskell\",\"marketing\",\"functional programming\",\"crossing the chasm\",\"developer community\"],\"quote\":\"although aimed at haskell programmers, is really about any technology looking to grow into the mainstream\",\"recommenders\":2,\