nomics (other)\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\"],\"tags\":[\"luxottica\",\"eyewear\",\"monopoly\",\"60 minutes\",\"consumer pricing\"],\"quote\":\"See this eye-opening 60 Minutes story on Luxottica\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"gJ5KV3rzuag\",\"title\":\"Should We Colonize Venus Instead of Mars?\",\"channel\":\"PBS Space Time\",\"summary\":\"A PBS Space Time episode asking whether Venus would be a better colonization target than Mars. It covers Venus's habitable altitudes, floating balloon habitats, and the term surfacism.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN links it in Mars-colonization threads as a concise case for Venus.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"venus colonization\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Cosmology & astrophysics\"],\"tags\":[\"venus\",\"mars\",\"space colonization\",\"floating habitats\",\"pbs space time\"],\"quote\":\"Don't miss the PBS Space Time episode suggesting we should colonize Venus instead of Mars which gives some good arguments and goes through the basics.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"gM95HHI4gLk\",\"title\":\"Salman Khan TED Talk 2011 (from ted.com)\",\"channel\":\"Khan Academy\",\"summary\":\"Salman Khan's TED 2011 talk on Khan Academy. He shows that it goes beyond video lectures to self-paced practice and analytics for teachers, and argues for filling gaps in understanding.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it to show Khan Academy's real model of mastery learning and teacher tools, often as a rebuttal to critics.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"online education\",\"categories\":[\"Education & learning\"],\"tags\":[\"khan academy\",\"mastery learning\",\"ted\",\"education technology\"],\"quote\":\"If you watch his (excellent) TED talk [1], you'll see that his organization isn't just about video lectures\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"gMqZR3pqMjg\",\"title\":\"The surprising pattern behind color names around the world\",\"channel\":\"Vox\",\"summary\":\"Vox explains the Berlin and Kay research showing that languages around the world tend to invent color words in the same order. It walks through the hierarchy and the debate around it.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as a clear, well-made summary of the linguistics of color naming and how culture shapes it.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"color naming linguistics\",\"categories\":[\"Language & linguistics\"],\"tags\":[\"color terms\",\"linguistics\",\"berlin and kay\",\"language and culture\",\"perception\"],\"quote\":\"there is a pretty well done video by Vox on how color names are influenced by culture\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"gSKzgpt4HBU\",\"title\":\"The True Nature of Matter and Mass | Space Time | PBS Digital Studios\",\"channel\":\"PBS Space Time\",\"summary\":\"A PBS Space Time episode asking what matter, mass, and energy really are, starting with inertial versus gravitational mass and what mass-energy equivalence means.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it, and the whole channel, as a clear and deeper-than-usual physics explainer.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"mass and energy\",\"categories\":[\"Fundamental physics\"],\"tags\":[\"physics\",\"mass-energy\",\"inertial mass\",\"pbs space time\",\"relativity\"],\"quote\":\"The YouTube channel PBS SpaceTime gives an excellent overview of these same ideas.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"ghUs-84NAAU\",\"title\":\"Testing 432 Hz Frequencies (and temperaments)\",\"channel\":\"Adam Neely\",\"summary\":\"Adam Neely tests the claims for tuning to A=432 Hz by trying the unusual tuning systems that its proponents' numerology requires. He compares how they sound against standard tuning and temperaments.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it whenever the 432 Hz versus 440 Hz debate or tuning systems come up, and as an accessible entry point to music theory for non-musicians.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"musical tuning systems\",\"categories\":[\"Music theory, synthesis & production\",\"Religion, belief & skepticism\"],\"tags\":[\"432 hz\",\"temperament\",\"music theory\",\"pythagorean tuning\",\"pseudoscience\"],\"quote\":\"As someone who hasn't taken any musical theory or similar, it was quite interesting to hear.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"giQ8xEWjnBs\",\"title\":\"Why SpaceX is Making Starlink\",\"channel\":\"Real Engineering\",\"summary\":\"Real Engineering explains why SpaceX is building Starlink, including the economics of satellite internet. It covers the latency advantage of light in vacuum over fiber for long-distance links.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a clear explanation of Starlink's purpose and the case that it can beat fiber on latency for long routes.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"starlink satellite internet\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Networking & internet infrastructure\",\"Tech industry & business models\"],\"tags\":[\"starlink\",\"spacex\",\"latency\",\"satellite constellations\",\"fiber\"],\"quote\":\"the whole video is worth watching\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"gwvA49ZXnf8\",\"title\":\"Call Between Alexey Navalny and FSB Officer Konstantin Kudryavtsev [English Subtitles]\",\"channel\":\"Bellingcat\",\"summary\":\"Bellingcat's publication of the recorded call in which Alexey Navalny, posing as a security aide, gets FSB officer Konstantin Kudryavtsev to describe the operation to poison him. It has English subtitles.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as a striking confession obtained through caller ID spoofing and social engineering.\",\"content_type\":\"news\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"navalny poisoning investigation\",\"categories\":[\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Law, policing & justice\"],\"tags\":[\"navalny\",\"fsb\",\"bellingcat\",\"social engineering\",\"novichok\"],\"quote\":\"But the best part is how he did it: caller ID spoof + social engineering.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"h2I8AoB1xgU\",\"title\":\"7 Minutes of Terror: Curiosity Rover's Risky Mars Landing | Video\",\"channel\":\"VideoFromSpace\",\"summary\":\"NASA's animated explanation of the Curiosity rover's Mars landing, which relied on a complex automated sequence taking about seven minutes. It features NASA engineers discussing the risks before the 2012 landing.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a gripping look at how hard Mars entry, descent and landing is.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"mars rover landing\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Robotics\"],\"tags\":[\"curiosity\",\"nasa\",\"mars landing\",\"sky crane\",\"entry descent landing\"],\"quote\":\"Here's a video that blows my mind every time I watch it.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"h5cm7HOAqZY\",\"title\":\"California's Renewable Energy Problem\",\"channel\":\"Real Engineering\",\"summary\":\"Real Engineering looks at the numbers for running California on renewables, focusing on the large energy storage needed. It argues about the cost of batteries and the role of other sources.\",\"why_hn\":\"Offered in energy and nuclear debates as a numbers-based walkthrough of renewable storage costs, though one commenter disliked its tone.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"renewable energy storage\",\"categories\":[\"Renewables, batteries & storage\",\"Power grid, heating & buildings\"],\"tags\":[\"renewables\",\"grid storage\",\"california\",\"nuclear\",\"batteries\"],\"quote\":\"Walks through the numbers on what it would take to run California on renewables + storage alone.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"hMKy52Intac\",\"title\":\"Xanadu Basics 1a - VISIBLE CONNECTION\",\"channel\":\"TheTedNelson\",\"summary\":\"Ted Nelson explains the original Xanadu hypertext idea of visible connection, the notion that links between documents should be shown and preserved. He argues that the Web and current document standards lost this concept.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as the author's own short explanation of Xanadu's core ideas, usually in threads on hypertext, linking and decentralizing the web.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"hypertext\",\"categories\":[\"History of computing\",\"GUI, HCI & interface history\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"xanadu\",\"ted nelson\",\"links\",\"transclusion\",\"web history\"],\"quote\":\"Ted Nelson recently did a series of videos on the important ideas in Xanadu. Start here\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"hOE6nVVr14c\",\"title\":\"Keynote - JSON Graph: Reactive REST at Netflix\",\"channel\":\"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)\",\"summary\":\"Jafar Husain's ACM keynote presents Netflix's JSON Graph and Falcor, which let web developers treat all cloud data as one virtual JSON model. It combines reactive programming with REST principles.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as an alternative take on the data-fetching problem GraphQL addresses, and as a clear argument for when RPC or graph models beat plain REST.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"api data fetching\",\"categories\":[\"Web development\",\"Software architecture & design\"],\"tags\":[\"falcor\",\"json graph\",\"netflix\",\"reactive programming\",\"rest\",\"graphql\"],\"quote\":\"gives a very nice summary of when and how you might prefer RPC to REST\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0}",
    ",{\"vid\":\"i70wkxmumAw\",\"title\":\"This giant model stopped a terrible plan\",\"channel\":\"Tom Scott\",\"summary\":\"Tom Scott tells how John Reber's plan to dam San Francisco Bay was disproved by the Army Corps of Engineers' giant hydraulic Bay Model in Sausalito. The model showed the plan would have been dangerously wrong.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a short, fascinating story of a scale model preventing a terrible engineering decision.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"bay model engineering history\",\"categories\":[\"Civil engineering & construction\",\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"san francisco bay\",\"hydraulic model\",\"army corps of engineers\",\"john reber\",\"tom scott\"],\"quote\":\"I learned of this plan via this short Tom Scott video. Fascinating.\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"ibqiet6Bg38\",\"title\":\"Я позвонил своему убийце. Он признался\",\"channel\":\"Алексей Навальный\",\"summary\":\"Alexei Navalny phones an FSB chemical-weapons specialist, posing as a senior official, and gets him to describe the 2020 Novichok poisoning and its cover-up. The video is in Russian; HN commenters point to English subtitles.\",\"why_hn\":\"Praised as a remarkable piece of social engineering, spoofed caller ID plus pretexting, that produced direct evidence of the poisoning.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"navalny poisoning investigation\",\"categories\":[\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Law, policing & justice\"],\"tags\":[\"navalny\",\"novichok\",\"fsb\",\"social engineering\",\"russia\"],\"quote\":\"But the best part is how he did it: caller ID spoof + social engineering.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"j4kI2h3iotA\",\"title\":\"The Part of History You've Always Skipped | Neoslavery\",\"channel\":\"Knowing Better\",\"summary\":\"A long documentary-style video arguing that slavery in the US effectively