te\",\"primary_topic\":\"history of yahweh\",\"categories\":[\"Religion, belief & skepticism\",\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"yahweh\",\"ancient israel\",\"canaanite religion\",\"religious history\",\"bronze age collapse\"],\"quote\":\"it was one of the few videos I’ve seen recently that really impressed me\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"mwrA5IRGpfU\",\"title\":\"Writing a Wayland Compositor in Zig - Isaac Freund\",\"channel\":\"Zig SHOWTIME\",\"summary\":\"Isaac Freund, author of the River Wayland compositor, talks about writing a Wayland compositor in Zig. He covers why he chose Zig over C and Rust and how Zig can wrap a hairy C library.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a phenomenal talk on Zig's C interop and on choosing between C, Rust and Zig for systems work.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"zig and wayland\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Linux & open-source ecosystems\"],\"tags\":[\"zig\",\"wayland\",\"river compositor\",\"c interop\",\"systems programming\"],\"quote\":\"I loved his Zig+Wayland screencast [1], where he explained very engagingly how Zig is able to embrace and extend a pretty hairy C library\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"nBNTAmLRmUg\",\"title\":\"Vintage Electronics - The Tefifon\",\"channel\":\"Techmoan\",\"summary\":\"Techmoan demonstrates the Tefifon, a vintage German audio player that combines elements of record and tape with a grooved elastic loop. He shows how it works and plays it.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN fans use it as the gateway to the Techmoan channel and praise it as one of the most fascinating obscure audio formats.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"vintage audio formats\",\"categories\":[\"Audio & video engineering\",\"Hardware (other)\",\"Consumer devices & gadgets\"],\"tags\":[\"tefifon\",\"techmoan\",\"obscure media\",\"vintage hi-fi\",\"audio formats\"],\"quote\":\"My gateway video was the one