iginal music video for Everybody's Free to Wear Sunscreen, a spoken-word piece built on Mary Schmich's 1997 column of life advice, produced by Baz Luhrmann.\",\"why_hn\":\"Posted as timeless, comforting life advice in threads about careers, aging, and uncertainty.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"life advice\",\"categories\":[\"Productivity & self-improvement\",\"Music performance & songs\"],\"tags\":[\"wear sunscreen\",\"baz luhrmann\",\"life advice\",\"spoken word\"],\"quote\":\"A lot of wisdom in a 5min song\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"sWgDk-o-6ZE\",\"title\":\"CppCon 2015: Sean Parent \\\"Better Code: Data Structures\\\"\",\"channel\":\"CppCon\",\"summary\":\"Sean Parent's CppCon 2015 talk on better use of standard containers and the goal of having no incidental data structures. It argues that proper containers can greatly simplify code.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters say it changes how you think about types and the STL, and makes a case for simple modern C++.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"c++ data structures\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Software architecture & design\",\"Algorithms & data structures\"],\"tags\":[\"c++\",\"stl\",\"sean parent\",\"containers\",\"cppcon\"],\"quote\":\"this one really made me aware of what just might be the best way to think about it.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"s_osQvkeNRM\",\"title\":\"Stephen Fry on the Joys of Swearing\",\"channel\":\"gsmokeyjoe\",\"summary\":\"A short clip of Stephen Fry defending swearing as a rich and essential part of the English language and rejecting the idea that it is unnecessary.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters post it in swearing and profanity debates as the best statement against taking offense at profanity.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"swearing and language\",\"categories\":[\"Language & linguistics\",\"Free speech, censorship & civil liberties\"],\"tags\":[\"stephen fry\",\"swearing\",\"profanity\",\"english language\",\"free speech\"],\"quote\":\"Stephen Fry says it best\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"snz7JJlSZvw\",\"title\":\"Telescope Building with John Dobson\",\"channel\":\"Dobson Astro-Initiatives\",\"summary\":\"A roughly 90-minute film of John Dobson building a Dobsonian telescope step by step, including hand-grinding the mirror.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended to anyone interested in telescope making as a guide from Dobson himself.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"telescope making\",\"categories\":[\"Woodworking, metalworking & workshop skills\",\"Cosmology & astrophysics\",\"3D printing, CNC & maker projects\"],\"tags\":[\"dobsonian\",\"john dobson\",\"mirror grinding\",\"amateur astronomy\",\"diy optics\"],\"quote\":\"Here's a 90 minute youtube video on how to build one, with John Dobson himself\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"suRDUFpsHus\",\"title\":\"Mad Men - The Carousel (Higher Quality)\",\"channel\":\"TomR35\",\"summary\":\"The Kodak Carousel pitch scene from the Mad Men season finale, in which Don Draper sells nostalgia through a slide projector. It runs about three minutes.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN holds it up as one of the best pitches ever, an example of selling feeling and nostalgia rather than features.\",\"content_type\":\"other\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"pitching and storytelling\",\"categories\":[\"Film & TV clips\",\"Product, marketing & sales\"],\"tags\":[\"mad men\",\"kodak carousel\",\"pitch\",\"nostalgia\",\"advertising\"],\"quote\":\"Mad Men's Kodak presentation in season one is one of the best pitches I've seen.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"tDacjrSCeq4\",\"title\":\"Shouting in the Datacenter\",\"channel\":\"Bryan Cantrill\",\"summary\":\"A two-minute 2008 clip from Sun's Fishworks team in which Brendan Gregg uses DTrace to show disk latency spiking while he shouts at a rack of drives. Bryan Cantrill narrates the demonstration.\",\"why_hn\":\"It is the go-to viral demo whenever HN discusses vibration, acoustic attacks, or sound affecting hard drives.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"disk latency and vibration\",\"categories\":[\"Software performance & optimization\",\"Hardware (other)\",\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\"],\"tags\":[\"dtrace\",\"hard drives\",\"latency\",\"sun fishworks\",\"acoustic attack\"],\"quote\":\"this entertaining YouTube video from 2009, in which someone demonstrates the effect by literally shouting at a rack of servers\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"tP-Ipsat90c\",\"title\":\"Randomness is Random - Numberphile\",\"channel\":\"Numberphile\",\"summary\":\"Numberphile with Simon Pampena on how humans misunderstand randomness, including coin-flip sequences, run lengths and the gambler's fallacy.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an accessible demonstration that people are bad at producing or judging random sequences.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"perception of randomness\",\"categories\":[\"Probability & game theory\",\"Recreational & visual math\"],\"tags\":[\"coin flips\",\"gambler's fallacy\",\"probability\",\"numberphile\",\"human bias\"],\"quote\":\"Here's a great video demonstrating how people tend to misunderstand randomness\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0}",
