g energy rather than time. He draws on The Power of Full Engagement and his work on stamina and sustained performance.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it in discussions of shorter workweeks and productivity, arguing that rest and energy matter more than hours.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"energy management and productivity\",\"categories\":[\"Productivity & self-improvement\",\"Management, leadership & organizations\"],\"tags\":[\"productivity\",\"work hours\",\"rest\",\"stamina\",\"leadership\"],\"quote\":\"It's worth watching this talk from the Leading @ Google series -\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"tyixMpuGEL8\",\"title\":\"Flight of the Navigator | VFXcool\",\"channel\":\"Captain Disillusion\",\"summary\":\"Captain Disillusion's VFXcool episode, led by Alan Melikdjanian, takes a 41-minute nostalgic look at how the visual effects of Flight of the Navigator were made. It covers early computers, motion control, in-camera effects and practical crafts.\",\"why_hn\":\"Strongly recommended as a detailed, entertaining history of 1980s CGI and film techniques, including the role of the Foonly F1.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"1980s visual effects\",\"categories\":[\"Animation & visual effects\",\"Film analysis & criticism\"],\"tags\":[\"vfx\",\"flight of the navigator\",\"cgi history\",\"motion control\",\"film\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend this video on the making of Flight of the Navigator.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"uY-u1qyRM5w\",\"title\":\"Richard Feynman Lecture -- \\\"Los Alamos From Below\\\"\",\"channel\":\"The Quagmire\",\"summary\":\"A 78-minute Richard Feynman lecture of anecdotes about working at Los Alamos on the Manhattan Project, followed by about ten minutes of audience Q&A in which he tells three safe-cracking stories.\",\"why_hn\":\"Strongly recommended for its funny, human account of Los Alamos, which one commenter calls almost a stand-up act.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"manhattan project history\",\"categories\":[\"Fundamental physics\",\"Military history & warfare\",\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"feynman\",\"los alamos\",\"manhattan project\",\"safe-cracking\",\"anecdotes\"],\"quote\":\"He gives an incredible account of his time there in the lecture (and almost stand-up-comedy act)\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"uYNzqgU7na4\",\"title\":\"Why are British place names so hard to pronounce?\",\"channel\":\"Map Men\",\"summary\":\"The Map Men explain why British place names are so hard to pronounce, tracing it to layers of Viking, Anglo-Saxon, Celtic and Norman influence, with a pronunciation guide.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an entertaining, short explanation whenever British place names or their linguistic history come up.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"british place names\",\"categories\":[\"Language & linguistics\"],\"tags\":[\"etymology\",\"pronunciation\",\"english language\",\"viking influence\",\"uk geography\"],\"quote\":\"The Map Men on YouTube did a short (8min) video on why pronunciation is hard and a guide\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"udPY5rQVoW0\",\"title\":\"Playing a Neural Network's version of GTA V: GAN Theft Auto\",\"channel\":\"sentdex\",\"summary\":\"Sentdex demonstrates GAN Theft Auto, a GameGAN-based neural network that recreates GTA V so the network itself is the playable environment. He shows the results and releases the code.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as an early, striking demo of neural networks acting as game engines and world models.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"neural network game simulation\",\"categories\":[\"LLMs & generative AI\",\"Machine learning & deep learning\",\"Game programming & engines\"],\"tags\":[\"gan\",\"gamegan\",\"gta v\",\"world models\",\"generative ai\"],\"quote\":\"This Y