},{\"vid\":\"wqu_IpkOYBg\",\"title\":\"Farbrausch - fr-041: debris. [HD]\",\"channel\":\"kb\",\"summary\":\"Debris by Farbrausch, the winner of the Breakpoint 2007 demo competition. All of its 3D visuals, textures and music come from a single 177 KB executable.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as the demoscene showpiece to show someone what extreme size-limited real-time graphics look like.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"demoscene\",\"categories\":[\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\",\"Computer graphics & rendering\"],\"tags\":[\"demoscene\",\"farbrausch\",\"procedural graphics\",\"size coding\",\"real-time 3d\"],\"quote\":\"If you want to really show off the demoscene, try Farbrausch - fr-041.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"x5Efg42-Qn0\",\"title\":\"Myopia: A Modern Yet Reversible Disease — Todd Becker, M.S. (AHS14)\",\"channel\":\"AncestryFoundation\",\"summary\":\"Todd Becker's Ancestral Health Symposium talk arguing that myopia is driven by near-work and can be reversed, covering the biology and epidemiology and experimental evidence for reversal by using weaker lenses.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters credit it as a life-changing talk, with some reporting reduced prescriptions after following the method.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"myopia reversal\",\"categories\":[\"Medicine & infectious disease\",\"Life sciences (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"myopia\",\"eyesight\",\"near-work\",\"prescription lenses\",\"ancestral health\"],\"quote\":\"I'm super thankful to have found out about this life-changing video by Todd Becker on how to reverse myopia\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"xKu2de0yCJI\",\"title\":\"AT&T Archives: Saul Bass Pitch Video for Bell System Logo Redesign\",\"channel\":\"AT&T Tech Channel\",\"summary\":\"The 1969 pitch film in which Saul Bass presents the Bell System logo redesign to AT&T, part of the largest corporate re-identity program in U.S. history.\",\"w