ng\",\"fedex\",\"air cargo\",\"hub and spoke\",\"supply chain\"],\"quote\":\"is a good Youtube video that discusses how overnight shipping systems like Fedex etc. have works.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"yG1OZ69H_-o\",\"title\":\"CppCon 2016: Chandler Carruth “Garbage In, Garbage Out: Arguing about Undefined Behavior...\\\"\",\"channel\":\"CppCon\",\"summary\":\"Chandler Carruth's CppCon 2016 talk tries to defuse the heated debate over undefined behavior in C and C++. He explains from the compiler writer's perspective why UB exists and how it enables optimization.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it whenever undefined behavior comes up, as the best explanation of the reasoning behind UB, though some dispute its framing.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"undefined behavior in C++\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Compilers, interpreters & program analysis\",\"Software performance & optimization\"],\"tags\":[\"undefined behavior\",\"c++\",\"compilers\",\"optimization\",\"signed overflow\",\"llvm\"],\"quote\":\"Chandler Carruth's talk on the subject was really useful for my own understanding of the reasoning behind UB\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"yQ6VOOd73MA\",\"title\":\"Your Brain: Who's in Control? | Full Documentary | NOVA | PBS\",\"channel\":\"NOVA PBS Official\",\"summary\":\"A NOVA documentary with neuroscientist Heather Berlin exploring the subconscious and what drives our decisions. It uses sleepwalking, anesthesia, improvised rap in an MRI and game theory to probe how much of the brain's work is hidden.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in threads on consciousness, anesthesia and perception as a fascinating look at how much of experience the brain constructs.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"neuroscience of the subconscious\",\"categories\":[\"Neuroscience & the brain\",\"Consciousness & cognition\"],\"tags\":[\"subconscious\",\"consciousness\",\"anesthesia\",\"perception\",\"nova\",\"brain\"],\"quote\":\"Both of these videos are great resources on how much of what you experience of reality is made up or filled in by your brain\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"ysa5OBhXz-Q\",\"title\":\"How Wolves Change Rivers\",\"channel\":\"Sustainable Human\",\"summary\":\"George Monbiot narrates how reintroducing wolves to Yellowstone after about 70 years set off a trophic cascade. The wolves changed deer behavior, vegetation recovered, and rivers changed course.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as the go-to example of how one keystone species can reshape an entire ecosystem.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"trophic cascades\",\"categories\":[\"Animals & nature\",\"Environment, agriculture & food systems\"],\"tags\":[\"yellowstone\",\"wolves\",\"keystone species\",\"ecosystem restoration\",\"rewilding\"],\"quote\":\"You need to learn about trophic cascades. Here's a quick intro\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"z_hm5oX7ZlE\",\"title\":\"KEYNOTE / Robert Erdmann\",\"channel\":\"PyCon US\",\"summary\":\"Robert Erdmann, a materials scientist at the Rijksmuseum, gives a PyCon keynote on the ultra-high-resolution imaging of Rembrandt's Night Watch. He covers the automated gantry camera system, the Python software that drives it, and the large volumes of image data involved.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as a technically jaw-dropping talk, and it is the standard reference whenever the Night Watch gigapixel images come up.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"heritage imaging with python\",\"categories\":[\"Python, Ruby & scripting languages\",\"Visual arts, photography & architecture\",\"Data science & statistics\"],\"tags\":[\"night watch\",\"rembrandt\",\"gigapixel imaging\",\"python\",\"rijksmuseum\",\"pycon\"],\"quote\":\"This was the first talk I immediately felt the urge to share with multiple co-workers & friends.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"zkTf0LmDqKI\",\"title\":\"Steve Jobs on Failure\",\"channel\":\"Silicon Valley Historical Association\",\"summary\":\"A two-minute clip from a 1994 interview with Steve Jobs by the Santa Clara Valley Historical Association. Jobs talks about failure and about how most people never ask for help, recalling that he simply called people to ask.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters return to it as a motivational reminder to not fear failure and to just ask for what you want.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"fear of failure and asking for help\",\"categories\":[\"Tech pioneers & interviews\",\"Productivity & self-improvement\",\"Startups & entrepreneurship\"],\"tags\":[\"steve jobs\",\"failure\",\"asking for help\",\"motivation\",\"career\"],\"quote\":\"Whenever I feel fear of failure, I watch this video, and it might help you too.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"zt0OQb1DBko\",\"title\":\"\\\"A (Not So Gentle) Introduction To Systems Programming In ATS\\\" by Aditya Siram\",\"channel\":\"Strange Loop Conference\",\"summary\":\"Aditya Siram introduces ATS, a statically typed ML-like language that compiles to C and offers type-safe pointer arithmetic and a full proof language. The Strange Loop talk shows off C interop, concurrency and verification features with non-trivial examples.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in Rust and systems-language threads as the best introduction to ATS, a language claimed to go beyond Rust's safety guarantees.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"ATS systems programming\",\"categories\":[\"Programming language design\",\"Logic & formal methods\",\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\"],\"tags\":[\"ats\",\"systems programming\",\"dependent types\",\"formal verification\",\"strange loop\"],\"quote\":\"I recommend watching this presentation for a good idea of what ATS programming is like\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"zxRgfBXn6Mg\",\"title\":\"Desert Storm - The Air War, Day 1 - Animated\",\"channel\":\"The Operations Room\",\"summary\":\"An animated account of Day 1 of the Desert Storm air war on 17 January 1991, covering the 2,775 sorties flown against Iraqi strategic targets in the first 24 hours.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a deeply researched, visual series that shows how overwhelming the coalition air campaign was.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"gulf war air campaign\",\"categories\":[\"Military history & warfare\"],\"tags\":[\"desert storm\",\"air war\",\"military history\",\"animation\",\"operations room\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend watching this series about it, no one has dug into history like the Operations Room channel\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"-2ZTmuX3cog\",\"title\":\"ARCHIVE TEAM: A Distributed Preservation of Service Attack\",\"channel\":\"textfilesdotcom\",\"summary\":\"Jason Scott of Archive Team describes how a loose band of volunteers rushes to copy sites like Geocities, Friendster and Yahoo Video before their owners delete them. The talk covers the tactics they use and the argument that this data is history worth saving.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it whenever a company shuts down a service and wipes user content, as an entertaining case for digital preservation.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"digital preservation\",\"categories\":[\"Internet culture & memes\",\"Hacker culture & free software\",\"History of computing\"],\"tags\":[\"archive team\",\"geocities\",\"web archiving\",\"data loss\",\"jason scott\"],\"quote\":\"gave a fantastically entertaining talk about how they saved Geocities, Yahoo! Video, and Friendster\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"-bYAQ-ZZtEU\",\"title\":\"Astroturf and manipulation of media messages | Sharyl Attkisson | TEDxUniversityofNevada\",\"channel\":\"TEDx Talks\",\"summary\":\"Investigative journalist Sharyl Attkisson explains how astroturf, fake grassroots campaigns funded by corporate or political interests, manipulates media messages. The TEDx talk is about 11 minutes.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as an introduction to shills, astroturfing and lobbyist influence on media, especially in threads about fake news and online forums.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"astroturfing and media manipulation\",\"categories\":[\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Free speech, censorship & civil liberties\"],\"tags\":[\"astroturf\",\"media bias\",\"lobbying\",\"journalism\",\"tedx\"],\"quote\":\"She also gave another amazing talk on corporate astroturfing and media manipulation [2]\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"-cEn_83zRFw\",\"title\":\"Rails World 2024 Opening Keynote - David Heinemeier Hansson\",\"channel\":\"Ruby on Rails\",\"summary\":\"DHH's opening keynote at Rails World 2024 in Toronto, where Rails 8 beta shipped. It covers built-in authentication, Propshaft, Solid Cache, Solid Queue, Solid Cable, Kamal 2 and Thruster, pitching the One Person Framework that needs no PaaS.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as a primer on modern Rails and as a rebuttal to cloud 'learned helplessness', worth watching even by non-Ruby developers.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"ruby on rails\",\"categories\":[\"Python, Ruby & scripting languages\",\"Web development\",\"Cloud, DevOps & reliability\"],\"tags\":[\"rails 8\",\"dhh\",\"kamal\",\"self-hosting\",\"web development\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend you watch the first half hour of DHH Rails World talk on Rails 8 even if you aren’t a Ruby dev\",\"recommenders\":6,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"-qCKR6wy94U\",\"title\":\"Opioids II: Last Week Tonight with John Oliver (HBO)\",\"channel\":\"LastWeekTonight\",\"summary\":\"John Oliver's second Last Week Tonight segment on the opioid epidemic, covering the role of