compare Chinese and US rail and infrastructure.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"high-speed rail in china\",\"categories\":[\"Transit, cities & urban planning\",\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\",\"Civil engineering & construction\"],\"tags\":[\"china\",\"railways\",\"infrastructure\",\"transportation\",\"public policy\"],\"quote\":\"Please, I urge you to watch this.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"0Rnq1NpHdmw\",\"title\":\"Scientific Studies: Last Week Tonight with John Oliver (HBO)\",\"channel\":\"LastWeekTonight\",\"summary\":\"John Oliver's Last Week Tonight segment on how media outlets report incomplete or untrue findings as settled science. It covers sensational headlines, small studies and pressure on researchers.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as an entertaining and sophisticated primer on reading science reporting critically.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"science reporting\",\"categories\":[\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Scientific method & science communication\"],\"tags\":[\"scientific studies\",\"media literacy\",\"john oliver\",\"replication\",\"sample size\"],\"quote\":\"John Oliver has a great segment called 'Scientific Studies' I'll link at the end of this post, everyone should watch this.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"0Z4aF-qiziM\",\"title\":\"Defcon 21 - Decapping Chips The Strike Easy Hard Way\",\"channel\":\"HackersOnBoard\",\"summary\":\"A DEF CON 21 talk by Adam Laurie and Zac Franken on decapping chips, covering how to remove chip packaging and image the die to read out contents such as ROM.\",\"why_hn\":\"Regarded as a favorite practical walkthrough of chip decapping, linked in threads on die shots, hardware backdoors and key extraction.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"chip decapping\",\"categories\":[\"Security & hacking\",\"Semiconductors & chip manufacturing\"],\"tags\":[\"decapping\",\"reverse engineering\",\"defcon\",\"die imaging\",\"hardware security\"],\"quote\":\"One of my favourite talks is Decapping Chips the Hard Way by Adam Laurie and Zac Franken\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"0rR9IaXH1M0\",\"title\":\"Jim Jefferies -- Gun Control (Part 1) from BARE -- Netflix Special\",\"channel\":\"Jim Jefferies\",\"summary\":\"A clip from Jim Jefferies' Netflix special BARE in which he comedically dissects American gun culture and gun control arguments.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a funny but surprisingly persuasive outsider take on gun control, mainly in gun-related threads.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"gun control\",\"categories\":[\"Stand-up & sketch comedy\",\"US politics & elections\"],\"tags\":[\"stand-up\",\"gun control\",\"jim jefferies\",\"us politics\",\"netflix special\"],\"quote\":\"I recommend listening to what Jim Jefferies had to say about gun control.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"15R2pMqU2ok\",\"title\":\"How to Enhance Your Gut Microbiome for Brain & Overall Health\",\"channel\":\"Andrew Huberman\",\"summary\":\"A Huberman Lab podcast episode on the gut-brain axis and how the gut microbiome affects the nervous system, hunger and overall health. It covers the pathways by which the gut influences the brain and practical steps for gut health.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an accessible neuroscientist's overview of gut microbiome science with practical takeaways.\",\"content_type\":\"podcast\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"gut microbiome and brain health\",\"categories\":[\"Nutrition & diet science\",\"Neuroscience & the brain\"],\"tags\":[\"gut-brain axis\",\"microbiome\",\"huberman\",\"neuroscience\",\"nutrition\"],\"quote\":\"I would highly recommend this podcast (neuroscientist Andrew Huberman) if anyone wants to learn more about improving their gut health\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"17KCHwOwgms\",\"title\":\"Dan Abramov   The wet codebase\",\"channel\":\"eswarnichtsmehrfrei\",\"summary\":\"Dan Abramov's talk on the wet codebase, using visualizations to show how removing all duplication too early produces wrong abstractions that are hard to unwind.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in DRY versus duplication debates for its visuals and its case that copy/paste can beat a wrong abstraction.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"abstraction and code duplication\",\"categories\":[\"Software architecture & design\",\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\"],\"tags\":[\"dry\",\"abstraction\",\"dan abramov\",\"software design\",\"refactoring\"],\"quote\":\"Seeing what a premature, wrong abstraction looks like visually was eye opening.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"17oCQakzIl8\",\"title\":\"China & Uighurs: Last Week Tonight with John Oliver (HBO)\",\"channel\":\"LastWeekTonight\",\"summary\":\"John Oliver's Last Week Tonight segment on the Chinese government's treatment of the Uighur people, covering the human rights abuses in Xinjiang and why they deserve attention.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as an accessible, well-made mix of education and entertainment for anyone wanting to understand the Xinjiang situation.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"uighur persecution in xinjiang\",\"categories\":[\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Free speech, censorship & civil liberties\"],\"tags\":[\"uighurs\",\"xinjiang\",\"china\",\"human rights\",\"last week tonight\"],\"quote\":\"John Oliver did an excellent piece on the situation of the uighur last week\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"1L3eeC2lJZs\",\"title\":\"Angry Voicemail We Got From an Alamo Drafthouse Customer\",\"channel\":\"Alamo Drafthouse\",\"summary\":\"Alamo Drafthouse posted an angry voicemail from a customer who was kicked out for texting in the theater. The theater turned it into a humorous in-house preview.\",\"why_hn\":\"It is cited as a viral example of Alamo enforcing its no-talking and no-texting rules with humor.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"movie theater etiquette\",\"categories\":[\"Arts & entertainment (other)\",\"Internet culture & memes\"],\"tags\":[\"alamo drafthouse\",\"texting\",\"theater rules\",\"viral video\",\"customer service\"],\"quote\":\"This video Alamo posted to youtube of an angry customer bitching about getting kicked out for texting is amazing\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"1W_mSOS1Qts\",\"title\":\"The Death of Affordable Computing | Tariffs Impact & Investigation\",\"channel\":\"Gamers Nexus\",\"summary\":\"A long Gamers Nexus investigation into how volatile US tariffs affect the computer hardware industry. It interviews manufacturers and sellers about costs, margins and why moving production to the US is hard.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it for concrete numbers on what tariffs do to small hardware businesses.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"tariffs and pc hardware\",\"categories\":[\"Tech industry & business models\",\"Consumer devices & gadgets\",\"Manufacturing & industrial processes\"],\"tags\":[\"tariffs\",\"computer hardware\",\"supply chain\",\"manufacturing\",\"gamers nexus\"],\"quote\":\"Best part is having a product manager show a spreadsheet of costs and margins and explain in real terms (\$\$\$) what tariffs do to their business.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"1WupH8oyrAo\",\"title\":\"Crow skiing down a roof\",\"channel\":\"Niko Niko\",\"summary\":\"A one-minute clip of a crow repeatedly sliding down a snowy roof on a small lid, apparently just for fun.\",\"why_hn\":\"Offered as vivid evidence that animals, crows in particular, play for pleasure and display intelligence beyond survival needs.\",\"content_type\":\"other\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"animal play and intelligence\",\"categories\":[\"Animals & nature\"],\"tags\":[\"crows\",\"animal behavior\",\"play\",\"bird intelligence\"],\"quote\":\"This video of a crow repeatedly \\\"skiing\\\" down a roof changed my view of how animals play\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"1tSqSMOyNFE\",\"title\":\"How We’re Fooled By Statistics\",\"channel\":\"Veritasium\",\"summary\":\"A short Veritasium video explaining regression to the mean and how ignoring it leads to wrong conclusions about punishment versus reward, medical treatments and sports streaks. It uses the example of flight instructors who believed criticism works better than praise.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters link it as the clearest short explanation of regression to the mean, especially for how it misleads people about feedback and statistics.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"regression to the mean\",\"categories\":[\"Data science & statistics\",\"Psychology & human behavior\"],\"tags\":[\"statistics\",\"feedback\",\"psychology\",\"cognitive bias\",\"veritasium\"],\"quote\":\"Veritasium explains it better than me.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"24OXzIRIiMQ\",\"title\":\"Alpha Centauri Quotes: Intro and Tech's 0-24\",\"channel\":\"uvwar\",\"summary\":\"Audio clips of the intro and technology quotes from the 1999 strategy game Sid Meier's Alpha Centauri, in male and female voices, covering techs 0 through 24.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN fans share it as a way to hear the game's philosophical, sci-fi quotes in sequence.\",\"content_type\":\"other\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"alpha centauri game quotes\",\"categories\":[\"Game history & retro gaming\",\"Gaming culture & analysis\"],\"tags\":[\"alpha centauri\",\"sid meier\",\"video games\",\"science fiction\",\"game writing\"],\"quote\":\"I find them to be timeless, and quite heady when listened to in sequence.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"2EWejmkKlxs\",\"title\":\"CppCon 2017: Chandler Carruth “Going Nowhere Faster”\",\"channel\":\"CppCon\",\"summary\":\"Chandler Carruth shows how to squeeze more performance out of already-optimized C++ code, covering how the CPU executes it. The talk goes into pipelining, branch prediction and speculative execution using benchmarks.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as the best presentation on how modern CPUs run code, and why speculative execution matters for performance.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"cpu performance tuning\",\"categories\":[\"Software performance & optimization\",\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Computer architecture & CPUs\"],\"tags\":[\"c++\",\"branch prediction\",\"speculative execution\",\"benchmarking\",\"compilers\"],\"quote\":\"The best presentation I've seen about CPU performance related to pipelining, branch prediction, and speculative execution\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"2FMBSblpcrc\",\"title\":\"How to use one paper towel | Joe Smith | TEDxConcordiaUPortland\",\"channel\":\"TEDx Talks\",\"summary\":\"A short TEDx talk by Joe Smith teaching how to dry your hands with a single paper towel. It shows a simple technique for cutting waste.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN treats it as a tiny practical life hack some adopt for good, while others mock it as peak TED.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"paper towel waste\",\"categories\":[\"Environment, agriculture & food systems\",\"Home, DIY & practical skills\"],\"tags\":[\"tedx\",\"life hack\",\"hand drying\",\"waste reduction\",\"sustainability\"],\"quote\":\"I actually improved my hand drying technique after the TEDx on it\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"2KZb2_vcNTg\",\"title\":\"Where Do Trees Get Their Mass?\",\"channel\":\"Veritasium\",\"summary\":\"Veritasium asks people where a tree's mass comes from, then explains that most of a dry tree's mass originates from carbon dioxide in the air. It combines street interviews with a short explanation of photosynthesis.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it as the go-to demonstration of how unintuitive mass conservation is, especially in weight loss and burning threads.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"photosynthesis and mass\",\"categories\":[\"Scientific method & science communication\",\"Biology & biotechnology\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"trees\",\"photosynthesis\",\"carbon dioxide\",\"misconceptions\",\"science education\"],\"quote\":\"Veritasium has a fun video demonstrating how unintuitive this is\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"2R07FL1wVo4\",\"title\":\"\\\"The Dangerous Truth About Protein\\\" - Janice Stanger, Ph.D.\",\"channel\":\"vshvideo\",\"summary\":\"A presentation by Janice Stanger arguing that protein is overhyped and that excess or the wrong kinds of protein are harmful. It promotes a whole-foods, plant-based diet.\",\"why_hn\":\"A few commenters cite it as a starting point for the claim that excess protein is harmful, though the claims are one-sided advocacy.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"protein and plant-based nutrition\",\"categories\":[\"Nutrition & diet science\"],\"tags\":[\"protein\",\"vegan diet\",\"nutrition\",\"health claims\"],\"quote\":null,\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"2SuvO4Gi7uY\",\"title\":\"Superpositions, Sudoku, the Wave Function Collapse algorithm.\",\"channel\":\"Martin Donald\",\"summary\":\"Martin Donald explains the Wave Function Collapse algorithm using Sudoku-like constraint solving and shows how he implemented it with Blender and Godot. It links demos and reference articles.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters recommend it as the clearest way to understand WFC, especially in threads about Townscaper and tiled content generation.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"procedural generation algorithms\",\"categories\":[\"Algorithms & data structures\",\"Computer graphics & 