raphics, constraints and objects, and as one of Alan Kay's favorite things to show.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"computing history\",\"categories\":[\"History of computing\",\"GUI, HCI & interface history\",\"Computer graphics & rendering\"],\"tags\":[\"sketchpad\",\"ivan sutherland\",\"alan kay\",\"computer graphics\",\"constraints\"],\"quote\":\"one of Alan Kay's favorite demos over the years has been to show folks Sketchpad,\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"4AC6RSau7r8\",\"title\":\"Money as Debt - Full Documentary\",\"channel\":\"Free Your Mind\",\"summary\":\"Paul Grignon's animated documentary presenting his view of how banks create money as debt and why that system requires continuous growth. It outlines the historical background of modern banking.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an approachable explanation of fractional reserve banking, with the caveat that it is biased.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"money creation and banking\",\"categories\":[\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"fractional reserve banking\",\"debt\",\"monetary system\",\"animation\",\"paul grignon\"],\"quote\":\"the first Money as Debt video [1] still makes the most sense to me\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"4P_kbF0EbZM\",\"title\":\"Stephan T. Lavavej “Floating-Point ＜charconv＞: Making Your Code 10x Faster With C++17's Final Boss”\",\"channel\":\"CppCon\",\"summary\":\"Stephan T. Lavavej's CppCon 2019 talk on implementing floating-point to_chars and from_chars in Microsoft's C++ STL. It covers the history of float-string conversion and the algorithms that make it much faster.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN calls it a surprisingly fun, approachable talk on a hard problem and cites it in floating-point threads.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"floating-point string conversion\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, 