t video in potholer54's climate series, giving a basic look at how climate scientists infer that man-made carbon gases are changing the climate. It is a short explainer meant to present the scientific evidence plainly.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN users point to it as a clear, evidence-based series to counter climate skepticism.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"climate science\",\"categories\":[\"Climate science & climate change\"],\"tags\":[\"climate change\",\"carbon dioxide\",\"global warming\",\"science communication\"],\"quote\":\"There is a great video series on YouTube by \\\"potholer54\\\" that shows the scientific evidence for it better than I can.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"5Dnw46eC-0o\",\"title\":\"John Rauser keynote: \\\"Statistics Without the Agonizing Pain\\\" -- Strata + Hadoop 2014\",\"channel\":\"O'Reilly\",\"summary\":\"John Rauser's Strata 2014 keynote argues that programmers can learn statistics quickly by simulating random processes and shuffling data. He explains p-values through resampling rather than formulas.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an excellent programmer-friendly explanation of p-values and statistical thinking.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"statistics for programmers\",\"categories\":[\"Data science & statistics\",\"Probability & game theory\"],\"tags\":[\"p-values\",\"simulation\",\"resampling\",\"data science\",\"bootstrapping\"],\"quote\":\"This is an excellent talk I attended a while ago that explains it very well from a programmer's perspective\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"5Dw3aKbw5Wo\",\"title\":\"Gaslighting Your Fans w/ Dolby ATMOS™\",\"channel\":\"Benn Jordan\",\"summary\":\"Musician and audio engineer Benn Jordan tries Dolby Atmos as a consumer, covering the theory of immersive audio, its business model, and home theater and headphone listening. He concludes it often falls short of the pitch.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it in Atmos and spatial audio threads as a knowledgeable critique of why the format rarely delivers.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"dolby atmos\",\"categories\":[\"Audio & video engineering\",\"Music theory, synthesis & production\"],\"tags\":[\"dolby atmos\",\"spatial audio\",\"audio engineering\",\"home theater\",\"music production\"],\"quote\":\"I found this video by Benn Jordan very enlightening about the whole Atmos nonsense\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"5JYp9eGC3Cc\",\"title\":\"39.08! McMurtry fan car breaks Goodwood Hill RECORD! | Festival of Speed 2022\",\"channel\":\"Goodwood Road & Racing\",\"summary\":\"A short clip of the McMurtry Speirling fan car setting a new Goodwood Hill record of 39.08 seconds at the 2022 Festival of Speed, driven by Max Chilton. It beat the previous timed shootout record set in 1999 and the outright record held by the VW ID.R.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a striking demonstration of fan-downforce EVs, with a run that looks glued to the track and almost sped up.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"electric fan car racing\",\"categories\":[\"Cars, EVs & motorcycles\"],\"tags\":[\"mcmurtry\",\"goodwood\",\"hillclimb record\",\"ev\",\"downforce\"],\"quote\":\"Watching it set the record for goodwood is mind blowing\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"5MdSE-N0bxs\",\"title\":\"Connections between physics and deep learning\",\"channel\":\"MITCBMM\",\"summary\":\"Max Tegmark's MIT CBMM talk on why deep learning works so well. He argues that the laws of physics and the symmetries in physical data make it compressible into small neural networks, tying physics to network structure.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a clear argument for why deep and cheap learning succeeds, often alongside the associated paper.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"physics and deep learning\",\"categories\":[\"Machine learning & deep learning\",\"Fundamental physics\"],\"tags\":[\"deep learning\",\"physics\",\"tegmark\",\"neural networks\",\"symmetry\"],\"quote\":\"physical data tends to have symmetries, and these symmetries make descriptions of the data very compressible into relatively small neural circuits\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"5MxH1sfJLBQ\",\"title\":\"How to achieve nanometer precision in space?\",\"channel\":\"Breaking Taps\",\"summary\":\"Breaking Taps explains how the cryogenic mirror actuators on the James Webb Space Telescope achieve nanometer precision using flexures. It shows a 3D-printed replica and how one motor handles both coarse and fine motion.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters repeatedly recommend it in JWST threads as a great explanation of clever mechanical design that is accurate and long lasting.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"precision mechanical design\",\"categories\":[\"Mechanical & precision engineering\",\"Space exploration & spaceflight\"],\"tags\":[\"jwst\",\"flexures\",\"actuators\",\"mechanical engineering\",\"cryogenics\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"5QwOpRh-IfI\",\"title\":\"Sample Breakdown: Daft Punk - One More Time\",\"channel\":\"TRACKLIB\",\"summary\":\"A short Tracklib video visualizing the disco sample that Daft Punk's One More Time is built from. It shows how the track is composed from the original material.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a striking visual breakdown of how the song was constructed.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"music sampling\",\"categories\":[\"Music theory, synthesis & production\",\"Music performance & songs\"],\"tags\":[\"daft punk\",\"sampling\",\"disco\",\"music production\",\"one more time\"],\"quote\":\"This video is a great visualization on how it's composed. Absolutely incredible.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"5RKbSi87