ng it teaches more than an article does.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"deep reinforcement learning\",\"categories\":[\"Machine learning & deep learning\",\"Game programming & engines\"],\"tags\":[\"deepmind\",\"atari\",\"demis hassabis\",\"dqn\",\"reinforcement learning\"],\"quote\":\"you learn more about the tech from a youtube video than from an article\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"EgiMu8A3pi0\",\"title\":\"A4 / V2 Rocket in detail: Turbopump\",\"channel\":\"Astronomy and Nature TV\",\"summary\":\"A very long, detailed look at the A4/V2 rocket turbopump, the steam-turbine-driven twin propellant pump system. It covers the peroxide and permanganate catalysis that drives the turbine. This is part 1 of a series on V2 components.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend the series for its in-depth, hands-on explanation of how V2 turbopumps and peroxide decomposition work.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"rocket turbopumps\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Mechanical & precision engineering\",\"Military history & warfare\"],\"tags\":[\"v2 rocket\",\"turbopump\",\"hydrogen peroxide\",\"rocket engines\",\"wwii engineering\"],\"quote\":\"this series of videos is definitely worth watching\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"EmKQsSDlaa4\",\"title\":\"How are holograms possible?\",\"channel\":\"3Blue1Brown\",\"summary\":\"3Blue1Brown explains how holograms record a 3D scene on 2D film, using wave diffraction and phase. The video includes demonstrations of several real holograms.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters call it the best explanation of how holograms work, and one says it transformed their understanding.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"holography\",\"categories\":[\"Fundamental physics\",\"Recreational & visual math\"],\"tags\":[\"holograms\",\"diffraction\",\"wave optics\",\"phase\",\"3blue1brown\"],\"quote\":\"this might be one of my most favorite videos ever single-handedly changing my understanding of holograms\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"EoWMF3VkI6U\",\"title\":\"Fun with ultracapacitors!!\",\"channel\":\"Afrotechmods\",\"summary\":\"Afrotechmods plays with 2600F ultracapacitors that can dump hundreds of amps, shorting them to vaporize bits of metal. Along the way he explains the three most important capacitor equations. The uploader warns that the capacitors are not designed to be shorted.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters use it as a vivid, math-backed demonstration of what ultracapacitors can do and why shorting them is dangerous.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"ultracapacitors\",\"categories\":[\"Electronics & circuit design\",\"Renewables, batteries & storage\"],\"tags\":[\"ultracapacitor\",\"capacitor equations\",\"electronics\",\"energy storage\",\"high current\"],\"quote\":\"This video is a good demonstration\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"Ep2-ohgFOys\",\"title\":\"Abolish Copyrights and Patents? A Soho Forum Debate\",\"channel\":\"ReasonTV\",\"summary\":\"A Soho Forum debate in which patent lawyer Stephan Kinsella argues for abolishing copyright and patents against law professor Richard Epstein. Both come from libertarian perspectives.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a substantive debate on intellectual property from two libertarian angles, with Kinsella as the abolitionist voice.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"intellectual property law\",\"categories\":[\"Law, policing & justice\",\"Free speech, censorship & civil liberties\",\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\"],\"tags\":[\"copyright\",\"patents\",\"libertarianism\",\"stephan kinsella\",\"richard epstein\"],\"quote\":\"Here is a debate on IP with two different libertarian perspective\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"FfDa8tR25dk\",\"title\":\"Chernobyl 3828\",\"channel\":\"TeleconStudio\",\"summary\":\"A Ukrainian documentary about the liquidators who cleaned radioactive debris off the Chernobyl reactor roof in two-minute shifts. It presents their firsthand accounts and footage of the work.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a moving, first-person account of the people who dealt with the worst of the Chernobyl cleanup.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"chernobyl cleanup\",\"categories\":[\"Nuclear power & fusion\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\",\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"chernobyl\",\"liquidators\",\"nuclear disaster\",\"reactor roof\",\"soviet history\"],\"quote\":\"Chernobyl 3828 is about the people\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"G0Q4UAiKacw\",\"title\":\"How the Higgs Mechanism Give Things Mass\",\"channel\":\"PBS Space Time\",\"summary\":\"A PBS Space Time episode on how the Higgs mechanism gives particles mass, prompted by Fermilab's heavier-than-expected W boson measurement. It goes beyond the usual pop-science treatment without heavy math.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as the best non-mathematical explanation of the Higgs field, deep but accessible to lay viewers.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"higgs mechanism\",\"categories\":[\"Quantum physics\",\"Fundamental physics\"],\"tags\":[\"higgs field\",\"particle physics\",\"w boson\",\"standard model\",\"pbs space time\"],\"quote\":\"about as deep as a lay audience can hope to surmount\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"GFosQtEqzSE\",\"title\":\"Sustainable Energy - Without the Hot Air with David MacKay\",\"channel\":\"Harvard University\",\"summary\":\"David MacKay, scientific advisor to the UK energy department, gives a Harvard talk on sustainable energy at macro and micro scale, drawn from his book Sustainable Energy Without the Hot Air. It stresses the land area renewables require.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an approachable, numbers-driven overview of what renewable energy would take.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"sustainable energy\",\"categories\":[\"Renewables, batteries & storage\",\"University lectures & courses\",\"Climate policy, solutions & debate\"],\"tags\":[\"david mackay\",\"renewable energy\",\"energy numbers\",\"land area\",\"climate\"],\"quote\":\"The author also gave a talk a few years ago that is very approachable[2].\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"GLG9g7BcjKs\",\"title\":\"President Trump: How & Why...\",\"channel\":\"Jonathan Pie\",\"summary\":\"Jonathan Pie delivers a satirical rant just after the 2016 US election, blaming the political and media establishment for the rise of Trump. It is a short, profane monologue in character as a frustrated reporter.\",\"why_hn\":\"Shared after the 2016 election and later as a pithy account of why Trump won and why political division needs to be moved past.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"2016 us election\",\"categories\":[\"Satire & parody\",\"US politics & elections\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\"],\"tags\":[\"jonathan pie\",\"satire\",\"trump\",\"politics\",\"polarization\"],\"quote\":\"I think Jonathan Pie encapsulated it perfectly just a few days after the election\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"GNKFSpJIBO0\",\"title\":\"Math Encounters -- Five Balls, Two Hands: The Patterns of Juggling -- Colin Wright (Presentation)\",\"channel\":\"National Museum of Mathematics\",\"summary\":\"Mathematician Colin Wright demonstrates juggling and explains the mathematics of juggling patterns, including notation that led to new throwing patterns. It is a public presentation at the Museum of Mathematics aimed at a general audience.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an entertaining way to learn math through juggling.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"juggling mathematics\",\"categories\":[\"Recreational & visual math\",\"Probability & game theory\",\"Magic, puzzles & curiosities\"],\"tags\":[\"juggling\",\"siteswap\",\"combinatorics\",\"colin wright\",\"recreational math\"],\"quote\":\"my fondness for this video that uses juggling to good effect to teach math in an entertaining way\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"GRYcSuyLiJk\",\"title\":\"Robert Sapolsky: The Biology of Humans at Our Best and Worst\",\"channel\":\"Stanford Iranian Studies Program\",\"summary\":\"A 73-minute Stanford talk by Robert Sapolsky drawn from his book Behave. It surveys the biological factors behind human behavior at its best and worst.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends Sapolsky as an exceptional storyteller and points to this lecture on the biology of human behavior and violence.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"biology of human behavior\",\"categories\":[\"Neuroscience & the brain\",\"Psychology & human behavior\",\"University lectures & courses\"],\"tags\":[\"robert sapolsky\",\"neuroscience\",\"behavior\",\"violence\",\"stanford\"],\"quote\":\"a talk where he explores various physical and environmental factors that influence human actions\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"GVT3WUa-48Y\",\"title\":\"ANIME ROCK, PAPER, SCISSORS\",\"channel\":\"Corridor Digital\",\"summary\":\"Corridor Digital makes a roughly seven-minute anime short using Stable Diffusion and related AI tools, based on a technique they teach in a longer tutorial. It was an early showcase of AI-assisted animation.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as an impressive example of what AI animation could do and of VFX artists adopting AI in their workflows.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"ai-generated animation\",\"categories\":[\"LLMs & generative AI\",\"Animation & visual effects\"],\"tags\":[\"stable diffusion\",\"anime\",\"ai video\",\"corridor digital\",\"vfx\"],\"quote\":\"the quality of the animation (modulo some