 an intuitive explanation of neural networks that shifts how people think about AI and language.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"AI and neural networks\",\"categories\":[\"Machine learning & deep learning\",\"AI safety, AGI & impact\",\"LLMs & generative AI\"],\"tags\":[\"geoffrey hinton\",\"neural networks\",\"backpropagation\",\"ai risk\",\"language models\"],\"quote\":\"Richard Sutton takes a different view in an interview with Dwarkesh Patel[2]\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"ImoQqNyRL8Y\",\"title\":\"The Incredible Sounds of the Falcon Heavy Launch (BINAURAL AUDIO IMMERSION) - Smarter Every Day 189\",\"channel\":\"SmarterEveryDay\",\"summary\":\"Smarter Every Day shares a binaural audio recording of the SpaceX Falcon Heavy launch made by Trevor Mahlmann, with explanations of the sounds including the sonic booms of the landing boosters. It is meant to be heard with headphones.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in launch threads as an immersive way to hear what a Falcon Heavy launch actually sounds like.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"rocket launch acoustics\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"falcon heavy\",\"binaural audio\",\"spacex\",\"sonic boom\",\"spaceflight\"],\"quote\":\"the sonic booms of the boosters coming into land are amazing, listen with headphones!\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"Iod6uwUGM2E\",\"title\":\"How does a Bowling Pinsetter Machine work? (Brunswick GS-X)\",\"channel\":\"Jared Owen\",\"summary\":\"Jared Owen's 3D animated breakdown of how a Brunswick GS-X bowling pinsetter works, showing its mechanisms for sweeping, lifting and resetting pins and balls.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an exceptionally well-made explainer of complex mechanical machinery.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"bowling pinsetter mechanics\",\"categories\":[\"Mechanical & precision engineering\",\"Animation & visual effects\"],\"tags\":[\"pinsetter\",\"3d animation\",\"mechanical engineering\",\"bowling\",\"how it works\"],\"quote\":\"some of the best I've ever seen, and relatively recent.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"IrabKK9Bhds\",\"title\":\"They Shall Not Grow Old – New Trailer – Now Playing In Theaters\",\"channel\":\"Warner Bros.\",\"summary\":\"The trailer for Peter Jackson's They Shall Not Grow Old, a WWI documentary built from restored, colorized archival footage and BBC interviews with British soldiers.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a way to see WWI footage restored so the war feels modern and real.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"world war i restored footage\",\"categories\":[\"Film & TV clips\",\"World history\",\"Animation & visual effects\"],\"tags\":[\"peter jackson\",\"world war i\",\"film restoration\",\"colorization\",\"documentary\"],\"quote\":\"It's really incredible and makes the war (which was only 100 years ago) feel much more modern than old black and white footage.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"IxuU5L2MEII\",\"title\":\"ai.bythebay.io: George Hotz, Self-Driving Lessons from Comma AI\",\"channel\":\"FunctionalTV\",\"summary\":\"George Hotz of Comma AI gives a 2017 conference talk on lessons from building a self-driving system. He argues about how driving should be defined and why the common approach to autonomous vehicles is flawed.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as a candid, contrarian view of self-driving approaches and the real limits of the business.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"self-driving cars\",\"categories\":[\"Self-driving & autonomous vehicles\",\"Machine learning & deep learning\"],\"tags\":[\"george hotz\",\"comma ai\",\"autonomous vehicles\",\"machine learning\",\"driving\"],\"quote\":\"George Hotz has a killer talk about why the general approach to autonomous vehicles is flawed. I highly recommend it.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"Iyp_X3mwE1w\",\"title\":\"A Complete Beginner's Guide to Electric Vehicles\",\"channel\":\"Technology Connections\",\"summary\":\"Technology Connections' hour-long guide to electric vehicles, covering costs, trade-offs and especially how little home charging power most drivers need.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an entertaining, in-depth beginner's guide that persuades skeptics that a wall outlet often suffices.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"electric vehicles\",\"categories\":[\"Cars, EVs & motorcycles\",\"Renewables, batteries & storage\"],\"tags\":[\"ev charging\",\"technology connections\",\"home charging\",\"ev costs\",\"beginner guide\"],\"quote\":\"I was particularly swayed by the technology connections video on this topic I watched before buying my first EV\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"JENdgiAPD6c\",\"title\":\"Ricardo Signes - 闇のEメール伝説\",\"channel\":\"yapcasia\",\"summary\":\"Ricardo Signes' YAPC::Asia Tokyo 2011 talk on the legends and horrors of email: how messy the SMTP and email standards are in practice. The first few minutes are Perl-specific, but the rest applies to anyone handling email.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points people to it as a funny and sobering warning about why parsing, validating, or implementing email software is far harder than it looks.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"email protocols\",\"categories\":[\"Networking & internet infrastructure\",\"Python, Ruby & scripting languages\"],\"tags\":[\"smtp\",\"email parsing\",\"email validation\",\"perl\",\"internet standards\"],\"quote\":\"There is is awesome talk about E-Mail by Ricardo Signes\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"JeB3JnKp8To\",\"title\":\"Pipe Organ (5-story instrument)\",\"channel\":\"Rob Scallon\",\"summary\":\"Rob Scallon explores a five-story pipe organ, the largest in the Midwest, with organist John Sherer. The half-hour tour covers most of the instrument and how it works.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an engaging look at how an organ works as a whole orchestra, in threads about organs and live-coding them.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"pipe organs\",\"categories\":[\"Music performance & songs\",\"Mechanical & precision engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"pipe organ\",\"musical instruments\",\"rob scallon\",\"organ mechanics\",\"music\"],\"quote\":\"You'll want to give a watch\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"JiNKlhspdKg\",\"title\":\"New Horizons in Music: Polyrhythms | Loop\",\"channel\":\"Ableton\",\"summary\":\"Adam Neely's Ableton Loop 2017 talk links rhythm, pitch and synaesthesia. He shows that polyrhythms sped up become chords, so tempo and pitch are related by ratios.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters recommend it for the mind-blowing connection between rhythm and pitch and as an approachable intro to music theory.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"polyrhythms and music theory\",\"categories\":[\"Music theory, synthesis & production\",\"Recreational & visual math\"],\"tags\":[\"polyrhythm\",\"adam neely\",\"pitch and tempo\",\"music theory\",\"synaesthesia\"],\"quote\":\"Highly recommend Adam's channel if you're interested in music/music theory.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"K3lP3BhvnSo\",\"title\":\"How the Fed's \\\"Money Printer\\\" Really Works\",\"channel\":\"Ben Felix\",\"summary\":\"Ben Felix explains how central bank money creation and quantitative easing actually work, and what they do and do not imply for asset prices and currency. He addresses the common belief that the Fed prints unlimited money and props up markets.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN users point to it to correct the 'money printer go brrr' view and as a clear explanation of how banks create money through loans.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"central banking and money creation\",\"categories\":[\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\",\"Investing & personal finance\"],\"tags\":[\"federal reserve\",\"quantitative easing\",\"money supply\",\"bank lending\",\"monetary policy\"],\"quote\":\"Highly recommend this video to understand and this channel in general\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"KbB0FjPg0mw\",\"title\":\"Lecture 1: Probability and Counting | Statistics 110\",\"channel\":\"Harvard University\",\"summary\":\"Lecture 1 of Harvard's Statistics 110 with Joe Blitzstein, introducing sample spaces, the naive definition of probability, counting, binomial coefficients and the sampling table.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended on Ask HN threads as a high-quality free probability course for relearning math or building an ML foundation.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"probability\",\"categories\":[\"Probability & game theory\",\"University lectures & courses\"],\"tags\":[\"probability\",\"counting\",\"statistics 110\",\"harvard\",\"combinatorics\"],\"quote\":\"I have used and can vouch for the high quality of all of them\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"KgzQuE1pR1w\",\"title\":\"Bill Hicks - It's Just A Ride\",\"channel\":\"Bill Hicks\",\"summary\":\"A short clip from Bill Hicks' final special, Revelations, in which he describes life as just a ride. It is a philosophical, calming monologue.\",\"why_hn\":\"Offered as a pick-me-up and calming perspective when people feel lost or stressed.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"stand-up comedy philosophy\",\"categories\":[\"Stand-up & sketch comedy\",\"Philosophy & ethics\"],\"tags\":[\"bill hicks\",\"stand-up\",\"perspective\",\"monologue\",\"life\"],\"quote\":\"Whenever I find myself feeling like you do right now, I watch this video from Bill Hicks\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"Kxryv2XrnqM\",\"title\":\"Clean Disruption - Why Energy & Transportation will be Obsolete by 2030 - Oslo, March 2016\",\"channel\":\"Tony Seba\",\"summary\":\"Tony Seba's 2016 keynote argues that batteries, electric vehicles, self-driving cars and solar will converge to disrupt energy and transportation. He predicts by 2030 all new vehicles will be electric and autonomous and that oil and other fossil fuels will be obsolete.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as a well-argued case that solar plus batteries and EVs will reach a tipping point sooner than mainstream forecasts expect.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"energy and transportation disruption\",\"categories\":[\"Renewables, batteries & storage\",\"Cars, EVs & motorcycles\",\"Futurism & technology and society\"],\"tags\":[\"electric vehicles\",\"solar energy\",\"batteries\",\"self-driving cars\",\"technology disruption\"],\"quote\":\"the linked reference is a well argued version of the near future of transportation and energy. Highly recommended\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"L1j93RnIxEo\",\"title\":\"Here's What's Preventing You From Finishing Projects\",\"channel\":\"Zack Freedman\",\"summary\":\"Zack Freedman gives advice on why makers fail to finish projects, including scrapping bad ideas, showing work publicly and writing a plan that keeps projects fun. It is aimed at hardware DIY but generalizes.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN finds the project-scoping rubric useful for programmers too and recommends it on finishing side projects.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"finishing projects\",\"categories\":[\"Productivity & self-improvement\",\"3D printing, CNC & maker projects\"],\"tags\":[\"procrastination\",\"project scoping\",\"diy\",\"motivation\",\"maker\"],\"quote\":\"the rubric he uses is sound for programmer-y stuff too\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"L_XJ_s5IsQc\",\"title\":\"Snarky Puppy - Lingus (We Like It Here)\",\"channel\":\"GroundUP Music NYC\",\"summary\":\"A live, overdub-free performance of 'Lingus' by Snarky Puppy, from the 'We Like It Here' DVD recorded in Utrecht. It features a Cory Henry keyboard solo.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend Snarky Puppy as proof that vibrant, progressive modern jazz is being made today.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"modern jazz fusion\",\"categories\":[\"Music performance & songs\"],\"tags\":[\"snarky puppy\",\"jazz fusion\",\"live performance\",\"cory henry\",\"groundup music\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend anything by Snarky Puppy.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"LnS0PfNyj4U\",\"title\":\"Dr Russell Barkley on ADHD Meds and how they all work differently from each other\",\"channel\":\"Adhd Videos\",\"summary\":\"Dr. Russell Barkley explains how different ADHD medications work and how they differ from one another, in a short clip.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends Barkley as the best resource on ADHD, with clear explanations of what prescription ADHD drugs do.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"adhd medication\",\"categories\":[\"Mental health & neurodiversity\",\"Medicine & infectious disease\"],\"tags\":[\"adhd\",\"russell barkley\",\"stimulants\",\"medication\",\"neuroscience\"],\"quote\":\"Dr. Russell Barkley has good explanations of what different prescription ADHD drugs do\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"M8F5hXqS-Ac\",\"title\":\"Safe Cycling Showdown - Good vs. Bad City Design - Plus 1 Minus 2\",\"channel\":\"Not Just Bikes\",\"summary\":\"Not Just Bikes compares the same cycling trip to a hardware store in Calgary and in Amsterdam, using a 'plus 1 minus 2' format. It shows how street design shapes how safe and practical cycling is.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends the channel for understanding why North American road design makes cycling dangerous and how the Dutch approach differs.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"cycling infrastructure\",\"categories\":[\"Transit, cities & urban planning\"],\"tags\":[\"urban design\",\"netherlands\",\"calgary\",\"bike safety\",\"suburbs\",\"not just bikes\"],\"quote\":\"Watch the bicycle infrastructure get better as he get out into the Amsterdam suburbs.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"MFol6IMbZ7Y\",\"title\":\"Defeating Ssl Using Sslstrip (Marlinspike Blackhat)\",\"channel\":\"TheSecurityTube\",\"summary\":\"Moxie Marlinspike's Black Hat talk presenting sslstrip, which defeats SSL in practice by intercepting the http-to-https redirect.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an entertaining talk and the original source on the stripping attack that motivated HSTS.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"ssl stripping attacks\",\"categories\":[\"Security & hacking\",\"Networking & internet infrastructure\",\"Cryptography\"],\"tags\":[\"sslstrip\",\"moxie marlinspike\",\"https\",\"hsts\",\"black hat\"],\"quote\":\"Very entertaining.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"MO0r930Sn_8\",\"title\":\"Richard Feynman Magnets\",\"channel\":\"nebulajr\",\"summary\":\"A short clip of Richard Feynman answering an interviewer's question about how magnets work, in which he explains why a why-question has no simple answer without a shared frame of reference.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN returns to it constantly as a classic on the difficulty of explaining fundamentals and the limits of analogies.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"explaining magnetism\",\"categories\":[\"Fundamental physics\",\"Scientific method & science communication\",\"Philosophy & ethics\"],\"tags\":[\"richard feynman\",\"magnetism\",\"explanation\",\"physics\",\"epistemology\"],\"quote\":\"Richard Feynman explaining magnets is one of the best layman explainers\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"MYucYon2-lk\",\"title\":\"Hillel Wayne - Beyond Unit Tests: Taking Your Testing to the Next Level - 