greenhouse effect was not politically controversial and the US came close to acting on climate. It covers Exxon's early climate science and the policy failures that followed.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an entertaining summary of early bipartisan climate action and corporate influence on research.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"history of climate policy\",\"categories\":[\"Climate policy, solutions & debate\",\"Climate science & climate change\"],\"tags\":[\"climate change\",\"exxon\",\"kyoto protocol\",\"us politics\",\"video essay\"],\"quote\":\"Climate Town has a great video essay on it\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"N6xLMUifbxQ\",\"title\":\"Kursk: The Epic Armored Engagement (2013)\",\"channel\":\"The National WWII Museum\",\"summary\":\"A panel at The National WWII Museum on the Battle of Kursk, moderated by Keith Huxen with historians Robert Citino and John Parshal. The discussion covers the armored engagement and the German, Soviet and US approaches to tank production.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it for its comparison of tank factory efficiency and the Soviet approach of building cheap tanks with short lifespans.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"battle of kursk\",\"categories\":[\"Military history & warfare\",\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"wwii\",\"tank production\",\"soviet union\",\"eastern front\",\"military history\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend it\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"NeopkvAP-ag\",\"title\":\"So... the minute hand shows progression — apparently we think of time in wildly different ways\",\"channel\":\"Technology Connextras\",\"summary\":\"A Technology Connections video essay on how analog and digital clocks shape different mental models of time, with the minute hand acting as a progress indicator.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it whenever analog versus digital clocks come up, as an idea that changed how commenters think about time perception.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"analog vs digital clocks\",\"categories\":[\"UX & UI design\",\"Psychology & human behavior\",\"Product & industrial design\"],\"tags\":[\"clocks\",\"time perception\",\"mental models\",\"technology connections\",\"design\"],\"quote\":\"Technology Connections has a very good video on this, and completely changed thinking\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"NiRrvxjrJ1U\",\"title\":\"The Liquid Metal Battery: Innovation in stationary electricity storage\",\"channel\":\"School of Convergence Science \",\"summary\":\"MIT's Donald Sadoway presents the liquid metal battery as a design for grid-scale stationary electricity storage, at an Imperial College London event in 2018. He covers the grid benefits of massive-scale storage.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN brings it up in energy storage threads as a promising scalable grid storage technology, and calls it worth the hour.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"grid energy storage\",\"categories\":[\"Renewables, batteries & storage\",\"Materials science\",\"Power grid, heating & buildings\"],\"tags\":[\"liquid metal battery\",\"donald sadoway\",\"grid storage\",\"batteries\",\"mit\"],\"quote\":\"It's an hour long, but it's well worth the time investment.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"NngCHTImH1g\",\"title\":\"The Future of Humanity's Energy No One Knows About | Terraform\",\"channel\":\"S3 | Science, Startups, & Stories\",\"summary\":\"A 20-minute S3 episode touring Terraform Industries, a startup making synthetic natural gas from air and solar power. It walks through the reactor, injection system, direct air capture and electrolyzer, plus the company's cost goals and next milestone.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as a clear, short tour of Terraform's synthetic fuel approach and goals.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"synt