k to Nim.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"combinatorial game theory\",\"categories\":[\"Recreational & visual math\",\"Probability & game theory\",\"Pure mathematics\"],\"tags\":[\"hackenbush\",\"surreal numbers\",\"nim\",\"game theory\",\"math visualization\"],\"quote\":\"I found the following video extremely useful and well-visualized\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"ZecQ64l-gKM\",\"title\":\"Lee Cronin: Origin of Life, Aliens, Complexity, and Consciousness | Lex Fridman Podcast #269\",\"channel\":\"Lex Fridman\",\"summary\":\"Lex Fridman interviews University of Glasgow chemist Lee Cronin about the origin of life, aliens, complexity and consciousness. The conversation centers on Cronin's assembly theory.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it in origin-of-life and complexity threads as a fascinating long-form introduction to assembly theory.\",\"content_type\":\"podcast\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"origin of life and assembly theory\",\"categories\":[\"Chemistry\",\"Biology & biotechnology\",\"Consciousness & cognition\"],\"tags\":[\"lee cronin\",\"assembly theory\",\"origin of life\",\"chemistry\",\"lex fridman\"],\"quote\":\"It really changed my naive perspective of life, and the universe.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"ZfuierUvx1A\",\"title\":\"Chaos Theory - Awesome 64k Intro! [720p HD]\",\"channel\":\"Lounger\",\"summary\":\"Chaos Theory is a 64k demoscene intro by Conspiracy and CNS that took second place at Assembly 2006, generating its graphics and music from a tiny executable.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people use it as a showcase of what fits in 64 kilobytes.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"demoscene 64k intros\",\"categories\":[\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\",\"Creative coding & generative art\"],\"tags\":[\"demoscene\",\"64k intro\",\"procedural graphics\",\"conspiracy\",\"assembly 2006\"],\"quote\":\"probably the coolest and most impressive one\"