st\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"self-driving and ai research\",\"categories\":[\"Self-driving & autonomous vehicles\",\"Machine learning & deep learning\",\"AI safety, AGI & impact\"],\"tags\":[\"andrej karpathy\",\"tesla autopilot\",\"transformers\",\"agi\",\"lex fridman\"],\"quote\":\"Anyone seriously interested in this question should listen to the Lex Friedman interview of Andrej Karpathy\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"cefnmjtAolY\",\"title\":\"Lenses, Folds, and Traversals\",\"channel\":\"Edward Kmett\",\"summary\":\"Edward Kmett's talk to the NY Haskell User Group on the lens library, building from fmap and function composition up to lenses, folds and traversals. It shows how these composable combinators access and modify parts of data structures.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN calls it dense but mind-blowing, the go-to way to understand lenses through algebraic derivation.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"haskell lenses\",\"categories\":[\"Functional programming\",\"Programming language design\"],\"tags\":[\"haskell\",\"lens\",\"traversals\",\"functional programming\",\"category theory\"],\"quote\":\"I found this talk by edward kmett incredibly helpful[0].\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"cfwwHa-7Ux8\",\"title\":\"A real person, a lot like you\",\"channel\":\"Derek Sivers\",\"summary\":\"A three-minute video from Derek Sivers, based on his book Anything You Want, about remembering that the people you deal with online are real people. It contrasts how we treat people face to face with how we treat them online.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in threads about online hostility as a short reminder to treat strangers as human beings.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"online civility\",\"categories\":[\"Productivity & self-improvement\",\"Internet culture & memes\"],\"tags\":[\"derek sivers\",\"empathy\",\"online behavior\",\"customer service\",\"short video\"],\"quote\":\"This is the video, I want everyone on internet to watch\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"clnozSXyF4k\",\"title\":\"Stargate Studios Virtual Backlot Reel 2009\",\"channel\":\"Stargate Studios\",\"summary\":\"Stargate Studios' 2009 virtual backlot reel shows before-and-after shots in which green screen and compositing replace locations in ordinary TV dramas and comedies. It shows how much of a seemingly real show is computer generated.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a demo of how routinely mundane TV scenes use green screen set replacement, even on TV budgets.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"virtual backlot visual effects\",\"categories\":[\"Animation & visual effects\",\"Filmmaking & video production\"],\"tags\":[\"green screen\",\"compositing\",\"vfx\",\"chroma key\",\"television production\"],\"quote\":\"This is an amazing demo reel of effects shots used in \\\"mundane\\\" TV shows\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"coFIEH3vXPw\",\"title\":\"Run containers on bare metal already!\",\"channel\":\"Bryan Cantrill\",\"summary\":\"Bryan Cantrill's Velocity NYC 2015 talk argues for running containers directly on bare metal rather than layering them on virtual machines. He covers the history of containers and how SmartOS runs Linux workloads via syscall emulation.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as an engaging and informative explanation of why containers on VMs waste resources and hurt performance.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"containers and virtualization\",\"categories\":[\"Operating systems & kernels\",\"Cloud, DevOps & reliability\"],\"tags\":[\"containers\",\"smartos\",\"bare metal\",\"joyent\",\"zones\"],\"quote\":\"he's an extremely engaging speaker, so not only are you likely to watch all of that 40 minute talk\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"csyL9EC0S0c\",\"title\":\"Programming is terrible—Lessons learned from a life wasted. EMF2012\",\"channel\":\"tef ebooks\",\"summary\":\"Tef's EMF 2012 talk on lessons from a career in programming, a candid and humorous look at why programming is so often terrible. Slides and a draft script are available online.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN lists it among its favorite programming talks and fantastic technical speeches.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"software engineering lessons\",\"categories\":[\"Software practice, open source & careers\",\"Software architecture & design\"],\"tags\":[\"programming\",\"software craft\",\"opinion\",\"emf camp\",\"abstractions\"],\"quote\":\"Both of these talks are in my top 5.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"czgOWmtGVGs\",\"title\":\"A New History for Humanity – The Human Era\",\"channel\":\"Kurzgesagt – In a Nutshell\",\"summary\":\"Kurzgesagt explains the Holocene or Human Era calendar, which adds 10,000 years to the current year to anchor dates to the start of human civilization. It argues this gives a more sensible frame for human history.\",\"why_hn\":\"Linked whenever year numbering or the Holocene calendar comes up as the accessible introduction to the idea.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"holocene calendar\",\"categories\":[\"World history\",\"Scientific method & science communication\"],\"tags\":[\"human era\",\"calendar\",\"holocene\",\"history\",\"kurzgesagt\"],\"quote\":\"Kurtzgesagt has a really great video about the subject\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"d0vY0CKYhPY\",\"title\":\"Pi and the Mandelbrot Set - Numberphile\",\"channel\":\"Numberphile\",\"summary\":\"Numberphile with Dr Holly Krieger shows how the digits of pi surprisingly emerge from the Mandelbrot set. A short, accessible math explainer.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended whenever the Mandelbrot set comes up, as a neat and surprising result.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"mandelbrot set and pi\",\"categories\":[\"Recreational & visual math\",\"Pure mathematics\"],\"tags\":[\"numberphile\",\"mandelbrot\",\"pi\",\"holly krieger\",\"fractals\"],\"quote\":\"My absolute favorite numberphile video is how pi occurs in a peculiar way with Riemann Zeta/Mandelbrot.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"d3kfEeMZ65c\",\"title\":\"Google I/O 2013 - High Performance Audio\",\"channel\":\"Google for Developers\",\"summary\":\"A Google I/O 2013 talk by Android audio engineers on why reliable, low-latency audio is hard on the platform. It covers problem areas across the stack, platform work underway and techniques apps can use.\",\"why_hn\":\"Treated as the definitive explanation of Android's audio latency problem, showing it spans the entire stack.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"android audio latency\",\"categories\":[\"Audio & video engineering\",\"Software performance & optimization\"],\"tags\":[\"android\",\"audio\",\"latency\",\"google io\",\"mobile\"],\"quote\":\"is a must-watch\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"dF_9YcehCZo\",\"title\":\"Saving Voyager 1! - Bruce Waggoner at !!Con 2024\",\"channel\":\"!!Con\",\"summary\":\"Bruce Waggoner of the Voyager team describes how engineers diagnosed Voyager 1's 2023 loss of telemetry and patched its flight software from 15 billion miles away. The talk covers the spacecraft's architecture and the scarcity of old documentation.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an amazing blind-debugging story with deep detail on 1970s spacecraft computing.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"voyager 1 debugging\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\"],\"tags\":[\"voyager\",\"nasa\",\"debugging\",\"legacy systems\",\"flight software\",\"bangbangcon\"],\"quote\":\"The talk is amazing and goes through the computer architecture of the spacecraft\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid