s\",\"History of computing\"],\"tags\":[\"bsd\",\"unix\",\"berkeley\",\"open source\",\"mckusick\",\"tcp/ip\"],\"quote\":\"but the whole thing is excellent.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"e08kOj2kISU\",\"title\":\"How to Speed up a Python Program 114,000 times.\",\"channel\":\"InfoQ\",\"summary\":\"David Schachter describes how he made a data-collection Python program run 114,000 times faster, drawing on decades of experience. The talk covers pipelining, cache effects and other optimization lessons.\",\"why_hn\":\"A favorite tech talk on HN for showing that hardware knowledge and generalist skills beat simply adding machines.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"performance optimization\",\"categories\":[\"Software performance & optimization\",\"Python, Ruby & scripting languages\"],\"tags\":[\"python\",\"optimization\",\"caching\",\"pipelining\",\"profiling\"],\"quote\":\"Humour, serious technical insight and a good reminder of why being a generalist is an advantage.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"e3K5UxWRRuY\",\"title\":\"35C3 -  The Ghost in the Machine\",\"channel\":\"media.ccc.de\",\"summary\":\"Joscha Bach's 35C3 talk offers an AI perspective on the soul, covering perception, mental representation, agency, consciousness and selfhood as things that can arise in a computational system like the brain.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters call it lucid and fluff-free, and point to Bach as one of the most interesting voices on AI, consciousness and philosophy.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"computational theories of mind\",\"categories\":[\"Consciousness & cognition\",\"AI safety, AGI & impact\"],\"tags\":[\"consciousness\",\"artificial intelligence\",\"joscha bach\",\"cognitive science\",\"philosophy of mind\"],\"quote\":\"the whole talk is incredibly lucid and contains zero fluff or BS\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"eC7xzavzEKY\",\"title\":\"T