r rather than a flaw in Tor itself.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"darknet opsec\",\"categories\":[\"Privacy, surveillance & cybercrime\",\"Security & hacking\"],\"tags\":[\"tor\",\"i2p\",\"silk road\",\"anonymity\",\"defcon\"],\"quote\":\"in most of the cases, it was bad OpsSec by the person, and had nothing to do with Tor\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"ef2jpjTEB5U\",\"title\":\"Bret Victor - Drawing Dynamic Visualizations\",\"channel\":\"Colin McDonnell\",\"summary\":\"Bret Victor's talk on Drawing Dynamic Visualizations. It argues that visualization tools offer either the directness of hand drawing or the dynamics of programmed graphics, and shows a tool that combines both.\",\"why_hn\":\"Counted among Bret Victor's best talks and recommended to anyone exploring direct-manipulation tools.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"data visualization tools\",\"categories\":[\"Data visualization & information design\",\"GUI, HCI & interface history\"],\"tags\":[\"bret victor\",\"direct manipulation\",\"dynamic visualization\",\"interface design\",\"programming tools\"],\"quote\":\"My favorite Bret Victor talk ever is\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"efPrtcLdcdM\",\"title\":\"GPT-4chan: This is the worst AI ever\",\"channel\":\"Yannic Kilcher\",\"summary\":\"Yannic Kilcher explains how he trained a language model on three years of 4chan's /pol/ board and let it post on the site. He evaluates how good the model was and discusses the ethics and fallout.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as the definitive account of the GPT-4chan experiment, used in debates on LLM bias, truthfulness and bots.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"gpt-4chan experiment\",\"categories\":[\"LLMs & generative AI\",\"AI safety, AGI & impact\"],\"tags\":[\"gpt-4chan\",\"language models\",\"4chan\",\"ai ethics\",\"fine-tuning\"],\"quote\":\"might be the c