ry. It runs about three hours.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a firsthand history of how Python became the language of scientific computing and ML.\",\"content_type\":\"podcast\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"scientific python history\",\"categories\":[\"Python, Ruby & scripting languages\",\"Data science & statistics\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"numpy\",\"scipy\",\"anaconda\",\"python\",\"travis oliphant\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend this bit of history from NumPy creator Travis Oliphant\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"gRRvjZ_XNog\",\"title\":\"DICKS: Do you need to be one to be a successful leader?\",\"channel\":\"Max Joseph\",\"summary\":\"Filmmaker Max Joseph's 35-minute video essay asks whether you have to be a jerk to be a successful leader. It draws on Adam Grant's givers and takers, Robert Greene and famous demanding directors.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a thoughtful critique of the great-leader-as-jerk myth in threads on difficult bosses.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"leadership and difficult personalities\",\"categories\":[\"Management, leadership & organizations\",\"Psychology & human behavior\"],\"tags\":[\"leadership\",\"givers and takers\",\"management\",\"video essay\",\"workplace\"],\"quote\":\"here's the best video I've found that breaks apart the idea of an \\\"asshole\\\"\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"gSKTfG1GXYQ\",\"title\":\"Charlie Marsh: uv: An Extremely Fast Python Package Manager\",\"channel\":\"Jane Street\",\"summary\":\"Charlie Marsh of Astral explains how uv, a Rust Python package manager, got so fast. He covers allocators, concurrency, zero-copy tricks and the challenges of Python packaging.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a fascinating technical account of the optimizations behind uv's speed.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"python packaging performance\",\"categories\":[\"Python, Ruby & scripting languages\",\"Software performance & optimization\",\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\"],\"tags\":[\"uv\",\"rust\",\"package manager\",\"sat solver\",\"performance\"],\"quote\":\"I recently watched a talk by the author of uv that was surprisingly fascinating\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"ggUduBmvQ_4\",\"title\":\"How Airlines Quietly Became Banks\",\"channel\":\"Wendover Productions\",\"summary\":\"A Wendover Productions explainer arguing that major airlines make much of their profit from loyalty programs and co-branded credit cards rather than flying. It frames airlines as quasi-banks that sell points in bulk, using United's pandemic-era loan as a hook.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it whenever airline economics or frequent-flier miles come up, since it clearly shows loyalty programs are worth more than the airlines themselves.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"airline loyalty program economics\",\"categories\":[\"Tech industry & business models\",\"Investing & personal finance\",\"Aviation & aerospace engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"airlines\",\"loyalty points\",\"credit cards\",\"finance\",\"business model\"],\"quote\":\"Wendover Productions had a good video about this, framed around United getting a loan during the pandemic\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"giYbq4HmfGA\",\"title\":\"ElixirConf 2023 - José Valim - The foundations of the Elixir type system\",\"channel\":\"ElixirConf\",\"summary\":\"José Valim's ElixirConf US 2023 closing keynote on the foundations of the Elixir type system, covering set-theoretic types and gradual typing with strong arrows.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as the best detailed explanation from the language's creator of how Elixir's new type system works and why.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"elixir type system\",\"categories\":[\"Programming language design\",\"Functional programming\"],\"tags\":[\"elixir\",\"gradual typing\",\"set-theoretic types\",\"type systems\",\"jose valim\"],\"quote\":\"If you're into watching talks, this will be well worth your time.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"goePYJ74Ydg\",\"title\":\"Simulating Green Beard Altruism\",\"channel\":\"Primer\",\"summary\":\"Primer simulates green beard altruism, where individuals recognize and help others carrying a shared marker, and shows how imposters affect its evolution. It is an animated evolution simulation based on published papers.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as part of Primer's strong series of evolution and emergence simulations.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"evolution of altruism\",\"categories\":[\"Evolution & genetics\",\"Probability & game theory\"],\"tags\":[\"green beard altruism\",\"evolution simulation\",\"game theory\",\"primer\",\"agent-based model\"],\"quote\":\"Primer, who's had a great string of genetic/evolution simulation videos\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"gqGEMQveoqg\",\"title\":\"A New Way to look at Networking\",\"channel\":\"Google TechTalks\",\"summary\":\"Van Jacobson's 2006 Google Tech Talk argues for rethinking networking around named data rather than host-to-host connections. He gives the history and the unsolved problems of the current internet architecture.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as the foundational talk on content-centric and named-data networking, and for its internet history stories.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"content-centric networking\",\"categories\":[\"Networking & internet infrastructure\",\"Software architecture & design\"],\"tags\":[\"van jacobson\",\"named data networking\",\"tcp/ip\",\"internet architecture\",\"ccn\"],\"quote\":\"There's an old tech talk that got me out of the IP-shaped box a lot of us are trapped in\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"gsffg5xxFQI\",\"title\":\"ClojureScript for Skeptics - Derek Slager\",\"channel\":\"ClojureTV\",\"summary\":\"Derek Slager's Clojure/conj talk argues that ClojureScript is a pragmatic choice for web development. He addresses common objections, recent improvements, tooling and use cases where it shines.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended to JavaScript skeptics as a persuasive case for ClojureScript, covering Closure Compiler optimizations and code-splitting.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"clojurescript for web development\",\"categories\":[\"Functional programming\",\"Web development\"],\"tags\":[\"clojurescript\",\"clojure\",\"javascript\",\"closure compiler\",\"web development\"],\"quote\":\"completely sold me on trying it out\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"hdUbIlwHRkY\",\"title\":\"The Concept of Language (Noam Chomsky)\",\"channel\":\"UW Video\",\"summary\":\"Noam Chomsky talks with the University of Washington's Upon Reflection about how languages change over time, why a national language is a modern idea, and how language is a system of communication rooted in human nature.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in threads on language purity and standardization for its clear take that languages are fluid and that national languages are constructed.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"linguistics\",\"categories\":[\"Language & linguistics\",\"Philosophy & ethics\"],\"tags\":[\"noam chomsky\",\"language change\",\"national language\",\"nation state\",\"philosophy of language\"],\"quote\":\"Here's my favorite talk on the subject given by Chomsky, highly recommend a listen\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"hpAMbpQ8J7g\",\"title\":\"RSA ANIMATE: First as Tragedy, Then as Farce\",\"channel\":\"Royal Society of Arts\",\"summary\":\"An RSA Animate adaptation of a Slavoj Zizek talk on charitable giving and ethical consumerism. It argues that buying products that bundle a charity donation can sustain the system that causes the problems.\",\"why_hn\":\"Frequently linked in threads on philanthropy, ethical consumption and billionaire giving as a short, approachable critique of charity.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"ethics of charity\",\"categories\":[\"Philosophy & ethics\",\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\",\"Social issues & culture\"],\"tags\":[\"slavoj zizek\",\"consumerism\",\"philanthropy\",\"cultural capitalism\",\"rsa animate\"],\"quote\":\"well worth a watch (10 minutes) and approachable by those without philosophical backgrounds\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"hpgK51w6uhk\",\"title\":\"America's Iron Giants - The World's Most Powerful Metalworkers\",\"channel\":\"Machine Thinking\",\"summary\":\"Machine Thinking tells the story of the Cold War Heavy Press Program, the giant forging presses that make parts for aircraft, missiles and turbines.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as an excellent introduction to massive forging presses, especially in threads about gigacasting and large manufacturing machines.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"heavy forging presses\",\"categories\":[\"Manufacturing & industrial processes\",\"Woodworking, metalworking & workshop skills\",\"Military history & warfare\"],\"tags\":[\"heavy press program\",\"forging\",\"metalworking\",\"cold war industry\",\"manufacturing\"],\"quote\":\"I first learned about these presses several years ago from the YouTube channel Machine Thinking which is excellent and unfortunately infrequent.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5}",
    ",{\"vid\":\"hs3piaN4b5I\",\"title\":\"Flexbox vs. CSS Grid — Which is Better?\",\"channel\":\"Layout Land\",\"summary\":\"Jen Simmons explains the difference between CSS Flexbox and CSS Grid, and when to use each. She makes the case that Grid does not replace Flexbox and most sites use both.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a short, clear rundown of one-dimensional versus two-dimensional layout.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"css layout\",\"categories\":[\"Web development\"],\"tags\":[\"css grid\",\"flexbox\",\"css\",\"web layout\",\"jen simmons\"],\"quote\":\"Here's a great explanation from Jen Simmons that really helped me understand the differences\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"hvk_XylEmLo\",\"title\":\"Work.\",\"channel\":\"Historia Civilis\",\"summary\":\"Historia Civilis traces the history of work and time discipline, comparing modern working hours with those of medieval peasants and the changes brought by clocks and industrialization. It draws on works such as Schor's The Overworked American.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it in work-hours and four-day-week threads as the source for the claim that people worked fewer hours before the industrial era.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"history of work\",\"categories\":[\"Labor, work & inequality\",\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"labor history\",\"medieval peasants\",\"work hours\",\"industrial revolution\",\"clocks\"],\"quote\":\"Here is an excellent video on the history of work.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"hz_mMLhUinw\",\"title\":\"The Superheterodyne Radio: No really, that's its name\",\"channel\":\"Technology Connections\",\"summary\":\"Technology Connections explains why the superheterodyne radio has its name and how mixing frequencies lets it tune stations well. It walks through the underlying wave phenomena and algebra and why the design solved a hard tuning problem.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people use it as the accessible go-to explainer for the superhet trick whenever radios or signal processing come up.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"radio receivers\",\"categories\":[\"Electronics & circuit design\",\"Information theory & signal processing\",\"Audio & video engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"superheterodyne\",\"am radio\",\"vacuum tubes\",\"signal processing\",\"heterodyning\"],\"quote\":\"This video is a great explainer (and I also highly recommend every other video on the channel)\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"iG9CE55wbtY\",\"title\":\"Do schools kill creativity? | Sir Ken Robinson | TED\",\"channel\":\"TED\",\"summary\":\"Sir Ken Robinson argues, with humor and stories such as that of choreographer Gillian Lynne, that education systems undermine creativity and should be changed. It is one of the most viewed TED talks.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN refers to it constantly in schooling debates, as a favorite talk or as the basis for arguments about creativity, though some commenters dispute its conclusions.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"education and creativity\",\"categories\":[\"Education & learning\",\"Ideas & learning (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"ken robinson\",\"ted talk\",\"schooling\",\"creativity\",\"education reform\"],\"quote\":\"I love this Ted talk\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"iGbC5j4pG9w\",\"title\":\"How an Average Family in Tokyo Can Buy a New Home\",\"channel\":\"Life Where I'm From\",\"summary\":\"A mini-documentary by a Canadian living in Japan explaining how an average family can afford a new detached house in Tokyo. It covers how houses are treated as depreciating assets and how Japanese zoning and building practices keep prices low.\",\"why_hn\":\"It is the standard citation in HN housing debates for showing that dense cities can still have affordable single-family homes.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"tokyo housing affordability\",\"categories\":[\"Transit, cities & urban planning\",\"Investing & personal finance\",\"Labor, work & inequality\"],\"tags\":[\"housing\",\"tokyo\",\"zoning\",\"urbanism\",\"real estate\"],\"quote\":\"a fantastic overview of housing for a nuclear family in Tokyo\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"iJfw6lDlTuA\",\"title\":\"Lecture 1 | The Theoretical Minimum\",\"channel\":\"Stanford\",\"summary\":\"Leonard Susskind opens Stanford Continuing Studies' Theoretical Minimum series with an introduction to quantum mechanics, a course for people who want real physics rather than popularization. It assumes some calculus and linear algebra.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends the series as an entertaining, serious route into physics for self-learners comfortable with basic math.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"quantum mechanics\",\"categories\":[\"Quantum physics\",\"University lectures & courses\"],\"tags\":[\"leonard susskind\",\"theoretical minimum\",\"physics\",\"quantum mechanics\",\"self-study\"],\"quote\":\"And he's entertaining as hell.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"iSVHp6CAyQ8\",\"title\":\"Why The World Relies On ASML For Machines That Print Chips\",\"channel\":\"CNBC\",\"summary\":\"CNBC gets a tour of ASML's cleanrooms in the Netherlands to see how its roughly \$200 million EUV lithography machines are built. It covers exploding molten tin, ultra-flat optics and why only one company can make these systems.\",\"why_hn\":\"Frequently recommended as a good, approachable overview of ASML and semiconductor equipment.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"euv lithography and asml\",\"categories\":[\"Semiconductors & chip manufacturing\",\"Tech industry & business models\"],\"tags\":[\"asml\",\"euv\",\"semiconductors\",\"chipmaking\",\"cleanroom\"],\"quote\":\"Good video on ASML and semiconductor fabrication equipment in general\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"ig_qpNfXHIU\",\"title\":\"Every Ruler Makes the Same Mistake When They Die\",\"channel\":\"CGP Grey\",\"summary\":\"CGP Grey, adapting The Dictator's Handbook, explains how rulers keep power and why succession causes trouble when they die. It is the sequel to his video on the rules for rulers.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a 101-level crash course on the keys to power, and says it changed how some viewers see political discourse.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"political power and succession\",\"categories\":[\"Politics & history (other)\",\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"dictator's handbook\",\"politics\",\"succession\",\"selectorate theory\",\"cgp grey\"],\"quote\":\"The 101-level crash-course on this is CGP Grey's video Death & Dynasties\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"ipVxxxqwBQw\",\"title\":\"Who Is Responsible For Climate Change? – Who Needs To Fix It?\",\"channel\":\"Kurzgesagt – In a Nutshell\",\"summary\":\"Kurzgesagt examines who is responsible for climate change, comparing historical, current and per-capita emissions by country. It argues that individual footprints are a distraction from larger responsibility.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a nuanced, data-backed treatment of emissions responsibility, made with Our World in Data.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"climate change responsibility\",\"categories\":[\"Climate science & climate change\",\"Climate policy, solutions & debate\"],\"tags\":[\"climate change\",\"emissions\",\"per capita\",\"carbon footprint\",\"our world in data\"],\"quote\":\"Perhaps you and they should watch the Kurzgesagt video made in conjunction with Our World in Data\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"iw17c70uJes\",\"title\":\"Future Crew - Second Reality (1993) [60fps]\",\"channel\":\"DemosceneVids\",\"summary\":\"A 60fps capture of Future Crew's 1993 MS-DOS demo Second Reality, one of the best-known pieces of the demoscene. It runs about 16 minutes of real-time graphics and music effects on PC hardware of the era.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters cite it as the landmark demo of the demoscene's golden era, and this capture lets people watch it without running it under DOS.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"demoscene\",\"categories\":[\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\",\"Computer graphics & rendering\"],\"tags\":[\"demoscene\",\"future crew\",\"ms-dos\",\"real-time graphics\",\"retro computing\"],\"quote\":\"Future Crew's 2nd Reality demo, for those that haven't seen it\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"j-kj2qwJa_E\",\"title\":\"Bruce Hauman - Developing ClojureScript With Figwheel\",\"channel\":\"ClojureTV\",\"summary\":\"Bruce Hauman presents Figwheel, a ClojureScript tool for live, interactive development with hot code reloading. He explains the main ideas, demonstrates how it works, and shares tricks for getting the most out of it.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people point to it as a very visual demonstration of what hot-reloading and interactive development can offer, and as an example of a great dev tool pitch.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"clojurescript live development\",\"categories\":[\"Functional programming\",\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\",\"Web development\"],\"tags\":[\"figwheel\",\"clojurescript\",\"hot reloading\",\"interactive programming\",\"developer tools\"],\"quote\":\"it's a very visual demonstration of what hot-reloading code and interactive development can bring\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"j6VlT_jUVPc\",\"title\":\"The Ultimate AeroPress Technique (Episode #3)\",\"channel\":\"James Hoffmann\",\"summary\":\"James Hoffmann demonstrates his AeroPress technique with a short recipe: 11g of coffee, 200g of just-boiled water, a 2-minute immersion, then a press. He explains why he skips rinsing, preheating and inverting.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN coffee fans cite it as a forgiving, repeatable recipe that gives good results.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"aeropress coffee brewing\",\"categories\":[\"Cooking & food\"],\"tags\":[\"aeropress\",\"james hoffmann\",\"coffee\",\"brew recipe\",\"immersion\"],\"quote\":\"I've found James Hoffman's aeropress technique to be fantastic though and much more repeatable\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"j7zzQpvoYcQ\",\"title\":\"The \\\"Last Lecture\\\" by Randy Pausch\",\"channel\":\"Gabriel Robins\",\"summary\":\"Randy Pausch, a Carnegie Mellon computer scientist and virtual reality pioneer who was dying of cancer, gives his 'Last Lecture' about achieving childhood dreams and living well. The recording is a full-length talk of about 104 minutes.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as an emotionally powerful life-advice talk and revisit it as a reminder of mortality.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"living well and mortality\",\"categories\":[\"Productivity & self-improvement\",\"University lectures & courses\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"randy pausch\",\"last lecture\",\"life advice\",\"inspiration\",\"memento mori\"],\"quote\":\"I often times revisit Randy Pausch's The Last Lecture[1] to act as a memento mori[2].\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"jOyfZex7B3E\",\"title\":\"Sega Saturn CD - Cracked after 20 years\",\"channel\":\"debuglive\",\"summary\":\"A look inside Dr Abrasive's lab as he engineers a flash-card replacement for the Sega Saturn optical drive after cracking its CD protection 20 years on.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an inspiring story of hardware reverse engineering and persistence.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"console reverse engineering\",\"categories\":[\"Speedrunning, glitches & game hacking\",\"Game history & retro gaming\",\"Embedded systems & DIY electronics\"],\"tags\":[\"sega saturn\",\"dr abrasive\",\"copy protection\",\"hardware hacking\",\"flashcart\"],\"quote\":\"Related and _very_ inspiring; how the Sega Saturn CD was cracked after 20 years.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"jQIHqkudgNY\",\"title\":\"Gambling and the desire machine | Pay to Win\",\"channel\":\"Jimmy McGee\",\"summary\":\"A 70-minute video essay by Jimmy McGee on gambling, addiction and game design, tracing horse racing, slot machines and collectible card markets. It is the first in a series on making money from games.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an engaging, well-researched look at the history of gambling machines and how games borrow their psychology.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"gambling and game design\",\"categories\":[\"Game design\",\"Gaming culture & analysis\",\"Mental health & neurodiversity\"],\"tags\":[\"gambling\",\"slot machines\",\"addiction\",\"video games\",\"monetization\",\"video essay\"],\"quote\":\"it's a genuinely interesting exploration on the murky history of video games and gambling\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"jlX_pThh7z8\",\"title\":\"WordTeX - A WYSIPCTWOTCG Typesetting Tool\",\"channel\":\"Tom Wildenhain\",\"summary\":\"Tom Wildenhain's SIGBOVIK 2018 presentation of WordTeX, a Microsoft Word template that mimics LaTeX typesetting output. It is a joke research project executed with serious effort.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people recommend it as an entertaining example of great effort on a trivial problem, and cite the template in LaTeX-versus-Word discussions.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"latex in word\",\"categories\":[\"Graphic design & typography\",\"Satire & parody\"],\"tags\":[\"wordtex\",\"latex\",\"sigbovik\",\"microsoft word\",\"typesetting\"],\"quote\":\"this one on WordTeX is excellent\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"jw8K460vx1c\",\"title\":\"Revolution OS\",\"channel\":\"Von Hash\