rol AI.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as a plain-language, well-conducted interview that explains what the FTC is doing about monopolization and antitrust.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"antitrust enforcement\",\"categories\":[\"Tech industry & business models\",\"Law, policing & justice\",\"AI safety, AGI & impact\"],\"tags\":[\"ftc\",\"lina khan\",\"amazon antitrust\",\"monopoly\",\"ai regulation\"],\"quote\":\"she pretty much sketched out (in the limited time she got) the main forces at work in the past 30 years of monopolization\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"otAcmD6XEEE\",\"title\":\"Procedural Programming: It Never Went Away — Kevlin Henney | Build Stuff\",\"channel\":\"Build Stuff - #1 Software Dev Conf\",\"summary\":\"Kevlin Henney argues that procedural programming never went away despite later paradigms such as OO and functional. He traces the history of structured programming and shows where procedural thinking still lives in modern code and why it matters for readability.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people recommend it as a fascinating history lesson showing that the field keeps rediscovering ideas from the 1960s.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"programming paradigms history\",\"categories\":[\"Software architecture & design\",\"Programming language design\"],\"tags\":[\"procedural programming\",\"structured programming\",\"software history\",\"code readability\",\"kevlin henney\"],\"quote\":\"tour of how all the best discoveries of the past decade or two really date back to the 1960s\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"ouAG4vXFORc\",\"title\":\"Why Do Mainframes Still Exist?  What's Inside One?  40TB, 200+ Cores, AI, and more!\",\"channel\":\"Dave's Garage\",\"summary\":\"Dave Plummer tours the IBM z16 mainframe from design through factory assembly, test lab, accelerators and water cooling. He explains why mainframes still exist and what makes them reliable.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an accessible tour of modern mainframes that compares them sensibly to ordinary server setups.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"ibm mainframes\",\"categories\":[\"Computer architecture & CPUs\",\"Cloud, DevOps & reliability\"],\"tags\":[\"ibm z16\",\"mainframe\",\"reliability\",\"hardware\",\"enterprise computing\"],\"quote\":\"This is an amazing 23-minute video by the Microsoft programmer who developed the Windows NT Task Manager, among other things.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"p8u_k2LIZyo\",\"title\":\"Fast Inverse Square Root — A Quake III Algorithm\",\"channel\":\"Nemean\",\"summary\":\"A walkthrough of the Quake III fast inverse square root, explaining where the constant 0x5f3759df comes from. It covers IEEE 754 floats, the bit hack that approximates a logarithm, and a Newton's method refinement.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an approachable explanation that makes the famous algorithm finally make sense.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"fast inverse square root\",\"categories\":[\"Algorithms & data structures\",\"Software performance & optimization\",\"Game history & retro gaming\"],\"tags\":[\"quake iii\",\"ieee 754\",\"floating point\",\"newton's method\",\"bit hacks\"],\"quote\":\"This video is approachable and explains it pretty well\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"pHsuIaPbNbY\",\"title\":\"Efficient Bayesian inference with Hamiltonian Monte Carlo -- Michael Betancourt (Part 1)\",\"channel\":\"MLSS Iceland 2014\",\"summary\":\"Michael Betancourt's lecture at MLSS Iceland 2014 on efficient Bayesian inference with Hamiltonian Monte Carlo. It covers MCMC concepts and motivation and the problems of sampling in high-dimensional distributions.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people return to it as a clear primer on MCMC and HMC and on why high dimensions behave counterintuitively.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"hamiltonian monte carlo\",\"categories\":[\"Data science & statistics\",\"University lectures & courses\"],\"tags\":[\"mcmc\",\"bayesian inference\",\"hmc\",\"high-dimensional sampling\",\"statistics\"],\"quote\":\"it was a fantastic primer on the basic concepts and motivations of mcmc, and later hmc\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"pMYYx_im5QI\",\"title\":\"Daniel Suarez: The kill decision shouldn't belong to a robot\",\"channel\":\"TED\",\"summary\":\"Novelist Daniel Suarez warns in a TED talk about autonomous robotic weapons and drones. He argues that taking the decision to kill out of human hands threatens democratic accountability and calls for a ban.\",\"why_hn\":\"Plugged repeatedly in AI and drone threads as a concise statement of the dangers of automated weapons.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"autonomous weapons\",\"categories\":[\"AI safety, AGI & impact\",\"Robotics\",\"Military history & warfare\"],\"tags\":[\"drones\",\"killer robots\",\"ai ethics\",\"ted\",\"daniel suarez\"],\"quote\":\"I often plug Daniel Suarez's great Kill Decision talk and book\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"pO4_Wlq8JeI\",\"title\":\"Solid Ground // Saša Jurić\",\"channel\":\"EMPEX Conference\",\"summary\":\"Sasa Juric's EMPEX talk demonstrates Elixir and Erlang's process model and what makes the BEAM runtime distinctive, such as fault-tolerant parallelism by design.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as the best short overview of why the BEAM and Elixir stand apart from other runtimes.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"elixir beam processes\",\"categories\":[\"Functional programming\",\"Distributed systems\"],\"tags\":[\"elixir\",\"erlang\",\"beam\",\"concurrency\",\"fault tolerance\"],\"quote\":\"It perfectly articulates what sets Erlang/BEAM/Elixir apart from other runtimes/languages.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"pX8BXH3SJn0\",\"title\":\"The NCAA: Last Week Tonight with John Oliver (HBO)\",\"channel\":\"LastWeekTonight\",\"summary\":\"John Oliver's Last Week Tonight segment on the NCAA, arguing that the organization profits enormously from college athletes while insisting they remain unpaid amateurs. It covers the money in college sports, including big-school athletic spending, and the case for paying athletes.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters cite it as a sharp, accessible primer on the NCAA's amateurism model and athlete compensation, including for readers outside the US.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"ncaa athlete compensation\",\"categories\":[\"Sports & athletics\",\"Satire & parody\",\"Labor, work & inequality\"],\"tags\":[\"ncaa\",\"college sports\",\"amateurism\",\"john oliver\",\"athlete pay\"],\"quote\":\"John Oliver has an excellent take on NCAA salaries issue\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"pxBQLFLei70\",\"title\":\"University of Texas at Austin 2014 Commencement Address - Admiral William H. McRaven\",\"channel\":\"Texas Exes\",\"summary\":\"Admiral William McRaven's 2014 University of Texas commencement address, built around lessons from Navy SEAL training. It famously opens with the case for making your bed every morning.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in life-advice and motivation threads as worth watching in full, especially for its point about starting small by changing yourself.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"commencement speech and discipline\",\"categories\":[\"Productivity & self-improvement\",\"Military history & warfare\"],\"tags\":[\"mcraven\",\"navy seals\",\"make your bed\",\"motivation\",\"commencement\"],\"quote\":\"Worth the whole watch\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"q0RX59G2jaA\",\"title\":\"What a Japanese Moving Company in Tokyo is like\",\"channel\":\"Paolo fromTOKYO\",\"summary\":\"A day-in-the-life video following a move between apartments in Tokyo using a Japanese moving company. It shows how the movers work and what the experience is like.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters recommend it for the movers' rigor and discipline, which they find oddly satisfying to watch.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"japanese moving companies\",\"categories\":[\"Documentaries & storytelling\",\"Arts & entertainment (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"japan\",\"tokyo\",\"moving\",\"daily life\",\"work culture\"],\"quote\":\"Seeing their rigour and discipline is like a visual ASMR video.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"qE7dYhpI_bI\",\"title\":\"Adam Savage's Epiphany on the Science of Measurement!\",\"channel\":\"Adam Savage’s Tested\",\"summary\":\"Adam Savage shows a set of Mitutoyo ceramic gauge blocks and uses them to explain metrology, the science of measurement. He argues that accuracy and precision work differently than most people assume, which changes how you think about every measuring tool.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a thoughtful, enjoyable 45-minute dive into measurement and the appreciation of precision.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"metrology\",\"categories\":[\"Mechanical & precision engineering\",\"Physics & space (other)\",\"Woodworking, metalworking & workshop skills\"],\"tags\":[\"gauge blocks\",\"measurement\",\"precision\",\"machining\",\"adam savage\"],\"quote\":\"I think you will thoroughly enjoy Adam Savage's (of Mythbusters fame) recent video on measurement.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5}",
    ",{\"vid\":\"qH6sSOr-yk8\",\"title\":\"C++ Seasoning\",\"channel\":\"aghuttun\",\"summary\":\"Sean Parent's GoingNative 2013 talk surveys new and overlooked C++ features and shows how to use them for simple, correct, clear code. It stresses using standard algorithms rather than raw loops.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended whenever the STL mindset or avoiding raw loops in C++ comes up, as an enlightening talk on expressive algorithms.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"modern c++\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Software architecture & design\"],\"tags\":[\"c++\",\"stl algorithms\",\"no raw loops\",\"sean parent\",\"goingnative\"],\"quote\":\"This one in particular is very enlightening\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"qJ7ZAUjsycY\",\"title\":\"How GPS Works, And How It Got Better Than The Designers Ever Imagined\",\"channel\":\"Scott Manley\",\"summary\":\"Scott Manley covers how GPS works and how civilian accuracy went from a planned 100 meters to about one meter. He explains the technology and the removal of restrictions that made this possible.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a solid history and explanation of GPS, especially when GPS outages or accuracy come up.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"gps\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Consumer devices & gadgets\"],\"tags\":[\"gps\",\"navigation\",\"satellites\",\"selective availability\",\"scott manley\"],\"quote\":\"Scott Manley has a nice video covering the history of GPS and how it works, well worth a watch\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"qPKj0YnKANw\",\"title\":\"Hawking Radiation\",\"channel\":\"PBS Space Time\",\"summary\":\"PBS Space Time explains Stephen Hawking's prediction of Hawking radiation and how black holes can emit radiation and slowly evaporate. It goes beyond the common particle-antiparticle analogy.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an accessible 