"why_hn\":\"HN readers point to it as a clear explanation of a theoretical fuel-free propulsion concept from a channel they respect.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"interstellar propulsion\",\"categories\":[\"Cosmology & astrophysics\",\"Space exploration & spaceflight\"],\"tags\":[\"halo drive\",\"black holes\",\"relativistic travel\",\"spaceflight\",\"astrophysics\"],\"quote\":\"Prof. Kipping is well known for his Cool Worlds youtube channel, which is fantastic.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"rbu7Zu5X1zI\",\"title\":\"How I animate 3Blue1Brown | A Manim demo with Ben Sparks\",\"channel\":\"3Blue1Brown\",\"summary\":\"Grant Sanderson of 3Blue1Brown shows his workflow for animating math videos with Manim, with Ben Sparks. He codes scenes live, including a Lorenz attractor, and walks through example scenes.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a rare detailed look at how 3b1b videos are made, including live debugging of his rendering engine.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"math animation with manim\",\"categories\":[\"Recreational & visual math\",\"Creative coding & generative art\",\"Animation & visual effects\"],\"tags\":[\"manim\",\"3blue1brown\",\"animation\",\"python\",\"live coding\"],\"quote\":\"I want to highlight the demo video [0], where Grant explains how he works with Manim.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"rimtaSgGz_4\",\"title\":\"DEF CON 31 - An Audacious Plan to Halt the Internet's Ensh*ttification  - Cory Doctorow\",\"channel\":\"DEFCONConference\",\"summary\":\"Cory Doctorow's DEF CON 31 talk describes how platforms decay in a pattern he calls enshittification. He lays out a plan to stop it through antitrust, interoperability and fixing the law.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in threads on big tech, monopolies and adversarial interoperability as the clearest statement of his argument.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"enshittification\",\"categories\":[\"Tech industry & business models\",\"Hacker culture & free software\",\"Law, policing & justice\"],\"tags\":[\"cory doctorow\",\"antitrust\",\"big tech\",\"interoperability\",\"platforms\"],\"quote\":\"I really recommend Cory's talk at DEF CON\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"rk6z1vP4Eo8\",\"title\":\"Should Google Go Nuclear? Clean, cheap, nuclear power (no, really)\",\"channel\":\"GoogleTalksArchive\",\"summary\":\"Robert Bussard's 2006 Google Tech Talk on inertial electrostatic confinement fusion, a compact approach he argued could be cheap and clean, using boron-hydrogen fuel without neutron radiation. It runs about 93 minutes and covers the physics, funding history and his proposed development path.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an intense, insightful look at Bussard's IEC fusion work, frequently cited in fusion threads for his claim that it could be developed for about \$200M.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"inertial electrostatic confinement fusion\",\"categories\":[\"Nuclear power & fusion\",\"Fundamental physics\"],\"tags\":[\"bussard\",\"fusion\",\"iec\",\"polywell\",\"google tech talk\",\"nuclear energy\"],\"quote\":\"it's an intense, fast-paced, insightful, and (likely) final public look into his mind, his work, and his character.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"rrkrvAUbU9Y\",\"title\":\"The puzzle of motivation | Dan Pink | TED\",\"channel\":\"TED\",\"summary\":\"Dan Pink's TED talk argues that traditional carrot-and-stick rewards often fail for creative work, drawing on the candle problem and social science research. He points to autonomy, mastery and purpose as better motivators.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it whenever money as an incentive comes up, as evidence that rewards can backfire for creative white-collar work.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"motivation and incentives\",\"categories\":[\"Psychology & human behavior\",\"Management, leadership & organizations\",\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\"],\"tags\":[\"dan pink\",\"candle problem\",\"intrinsic motivation\",\"incentives\",\"management\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend taking a look at the work of Daniel Pink related to money as an incentive.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"rtR63-ecUNo\",\"title\":\"How To Draw Mushrooms On An Oscilloscope With Sound\",\"channel\":\"Jellybean Fenderson\",\"summary\":\"Jerobeam Fenderson shows how to draw a mushroom on an oscilloscope in XY mode using stereo audio, then animates it by modulating with a larger wave. Pd and Max4Live patches are provided.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN finds it mesmerizing and uses it to build intuition for waveforms and oscilloscope XY drawing.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"oscilloscope art\",\"categories\":[\"Creative coding & generative art\",\"Electronics & circuit design\",\"Audio & video engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"oscilloscope\",\"xy mode\",\"lissajous\",\"audio visualization\",\"stereo sound\"],\"quote\":\"This was amazing to me: How To Draw Mushrooms On An Oscilloscope With Sound\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"rv-mFSoZOkE\",\"title\":\"Is Nuclear Waste Really Waste?\",\"channel\":\"Google TechTalks\",\"summary\":\"In a 2010 Google Tech Talk, Kirk Sorensen gives an economic analysis of what spent nuclear fuel actually contains. He argues it is mostly valuable material that can be partitioned and reused, not just waste to be isolated for 100,000 years.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN readers recommend it as the best explanation of what nuclear waste really is and how much of it is reusable fuel.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"nuclear waste\",\"categories\":[\"Nuclear power & fusion\"],\"tags\":[\"nuclear fuel\",\"spent fuel\",\"thorium\",\"reactors\",\"energy\"],\"quote\":\"This talk from 2010 is really amazing at understanding what 'nuclear waste' actually is and what it will be.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"s254IPHXgVA\",\"title\":\"Jancovici : Will technology save us from Climate Change ? MIT Media Lab - 23/02/2021\",\"channel\":\"Jean-Marc Jancovici\",\"summary\":\"Jean-Marc Jancovici gives an MIT Media Lab talk on whether technology can save us from climate change. He argues from a physical view of energy that economic growth, energy use and climate impact are tightly linked.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in climate and energy threads as a numbers-based explanation of why energy underlies growth and emissions.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"energy and climate\",\"categories\":[\"Climate policy, solutions & debate\",\"Nuclear power & fusion\",\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\"],\"tags\":[\"jancovici\",\"energy economics\",\"climate change\",\"growth\",\"nuclear\"],\"quote\":\"Interesting related presentation on what is energy and how it relates to the economy from a physical point of view\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"s8nFqwOho-s\",\"title\":\"NVScene 2015 Session: How to Create Content with Signed Distance Functions (Johann Korndörfer)\",\"channel\":\"NVScene\",\"summary\":\"Johann Korndorfer's NVScene 2015 talk on building content with signed distance functions. It focuses on patterns that make SDF modelling more structured, arguing that SDFs capture a shape's essence like vector graphics do compared with polygons or voxels.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an excellent talk from a demoscene practitioner on how to build sophisticated scenes from distance functions.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"signed distance functions\",\"categories\":[\"Computer graphics & rendering\",\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\",\"Creative coding & generative art\"],\"tags\":[\"sdf\",\"demoscene\",\"raymarching\",\"procedural modelling\",\"shaders\"],\"quote\":\"this is an excellent talk on the subject\",\"re