mulators.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as the standard example of what cycle-exact, hardware-level programming can achieve on ancient machines, from the colors it produces to its PC speaker audio.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"demoscene\",\"categories\":[\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\"],\"tags\":[\"ibm pc\",\"cga\",\"retrocomputing\",\"8088\",\"pc speaker\"],\"quote\":\"The most amazing thing I've heard done with a PC speaker is in the last part of this equally amazing demo\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"yY1FSsUV-8c\",\"title\":\"Andrew Sorensen Keynote: \\\"The Concert Programmer\\\" - OSCON 2014\",\"channel\":\"O'Reilly\",\"summary\":\"Andrew Sorensen's OSCON 2014 keynote in which he live-codes generative music on stage using his Impromptu environment while narrating his computational and musical choices. It imagines concert programmers as a performing art.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters regard it as an inspiring, all-time favorite demonstration of live coding music.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"live coding music\",\"categories\":[\"Creative coding & generative art\",\"Music theory, synthesis & production\"],\"tags\":[\"live coding\",\"andrew sorensen\",\"generative music\",\"impromptu\",\"creative computing\"],\"quote\":\"This video of one of his presentations on Impromptu is one of my all-time favorite programming talks\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"ydyztGZnbNs\",\"title\":\"Oculus Connect 2: Live Coding Session with John Carmack\",\"channel\":\"Meta VR\",\"summary\":\"John Carmack live-codes a simple VR application at Oculus Connect 2 using a Racket-based environment for rapid development and deployment on Gear VR.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited for watching Carmack code fluently and for the fast iteration cycle of Racket-based VR scripting.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"vr live coding\",\"categories\":[\"VR, AR & s