d rebuttal of Dark Forest axioms, and recommend his wider Fermi Paradox series.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"fermi paradox\",\"categories\":[\"Cosmology & astrophysics\",\"Probability & game theory\"],\"tags\":[\"dark forest\",\"seti\",\"cixin liu\",\"alien civilizations\",\"game theory\"],\"quote\":\"His entire library on the Fermi Paradox is worth watching.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"ztspvPYybIY\",\"title\":\"Ryan Dahl: Original Node.js presentation\",\"channel\":\"stri8ted\",\"summary\":\"Ryan Dahl's first presentation of Node.js at JSConf 2009. He pitches event-driven, non-blocking I/O as the motivation, rather than JavaScript itself.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a classic dev tool pitch with palpable energy, and cites it for why Node was created.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"nodejs origins\",\"categories\":[\"Web development\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"node.js\",\"ryan dahl\",\"async io\",\"jsconf\",\"javascript\"],\"quote\":\"There is a sort of palpable energy in (Ryan Dahl) node.js original presentation.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.5},{\"vid\":\"zz4YVJ4aRfg\",\"title\":\"Sulforaphane and Its Effects on Cancer, Mortality, Aging, Brain and Behavior, Heart Disease & More\",\"channel\":\"FoundMyFitness\",\"summary\":\"Rhonda Patrick of FoundMyFitness makes a case for isothiocyanates such as sulforaphane from cruciferous vegetables and broccoli sprouts. It covers cancer, aging, heart disease, brain and behavior, and neurodegeneration, with chapter timestamps.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a science-backed overview of sulforaphane's health effects, particularly for cancer.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"sulforaphane and health\",\"categories\":[\"Nutrition & diet science\",\"Medicine & infectious disease\",\"Fitness, sleep & longevity\"],\"tags\":[\"sulforaphane\",\"broccoli 