g.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters hold it up as proof that 2600 programming is alive in the demoscene and as one of the most impressive demos ever made on the hardware.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"atari 2600 demoscene\",\"categories\":[\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\"],\"tags\":[\"atari 2600\",\"demoscene\",\"retro hardware\",\"bankswitching\",\"revision 2014\"],\"quote\":\"2600 programming is alive in the demo scene. This was just created in 2014 and is completely insane\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"06yy88tLWlg\",\"title\":\"WOKE BRANDS\",\"channel\":\"hbomberguy\",\"summary\":\"hbomberguy examines whether a product can be truly progressive, looking at brands that adopt social causes in their marketing, with the Gillette ad as a prompt. It argues the behavior is driven by profit, not politics.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in threads on corporate politics, outrage and branding as an explanation of how companies use controversy and social stances for profit.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"brand activism\",\"categories\":[\"Product, marketing & sales\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Social issues & culture\"],\"tags\":[\"marketing\",\"woke brands\",\"advertising\",\"gillette\",\"capitalism\"],\"quote\":\"a very poignant discussion of the problematic underpinnings of brands adopting a particular aspect of a \\\"personality\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"0ifChJ0nJfM\",\"title\":\"Learn to Paint with Mathematics\",\"channel\":\"Inigo Quilez\",\"summary\":\"Inigo Quilez live-codes a painting using only mathematics in a shader, building it up step by step. The linked Shadertoy source shows the result.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as the most beginner-friendly way into shader programming and procedural graphics.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"shader programming\",\"categories\":[\"Creative coding & generative art\",\"Computer